WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:54.335 --> 00:00:58.294
PLANET: CHITON
POLITICAL REGIME: DICTATORSHIP


00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:03.459
LEADER: ADMIRAL SKORBA
POPULATION: 250,000


00:01:05.709 --> 00:01:08.876
POPULATION: 250,001


00:01:22.959 --> 00:01:24.918
Eureka, it worked!


00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:27.708
It worked!


00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:30.250
Oh, he's beautiful!


00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:33.208
He looks like a normal baby.


00:01:39.457 --> 00:01:41.041
It can't be them.


00:01:41.291 --> 00:01:44.125
They can't have found out so soon.


00:01:46.417 --> 00:01:49.417
-We have to hide him, Jan!
-They'll end up finding him.


00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:50.750
So...?


00:01:51.666 --> 00:01:52.916
There's only one thing we can do.


00:02:07.415 --> 00:02:08.498
They're here.


00:02:14.541 --> 00:02:16.956
-Good.
-You'll free us from them.


00:02:17.123 --> 00:02:18.331
Some day.


00:02:24.956 --> 00:02:27.998
You'll be safe here.
It's the planet's most advanced zone.


00:02:44.663 --> 00:02:47.664
When you grow up,
you'll come back to save us.


00:02:54.996 --> 00:02:58.454
-Get out of my lab, you rats!
-Go back to your sewers.


00:03:09.703 --> 00:03:12.537
First of all, good morning.


00:03:17.996 --> 00:03:20.245
I know everything.
Don't waste my time.


00:03:20.537 --> 00:03:24.412
-He's my son!
-No, he's an experiment.


00:03:24.787 --> 00:03:26.995
-Where did you put him?
-Where you can't find him.


00:03:27.162 --> 00:03:31.662
Don't make me push the button
and end this once and for all.


00:03:32.494 --> 00:03:33.494
I can help.


00:03:34.036 --> 00:03:36.577
I've no time for nonsense, Agata.


00:03:36.744 --> 00:03:39.619
But Dad, my cousin Sigfred
is the same age as me


00:03:39.702 --> 00:03:41.119
and they let him torture.


00:03:41.202 --> 00:03:43.452
Remember when I asked you


00:03:43.494 --> 00:03:46.535
to find all the pets on this planet
to annihilate them...


00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:48.868
and you hid some of them?


00:03:48.952 --> 00:03:51.452
I felt sorry for them,
but I've changed, I'm mature.


00:03:51.494 --> 00:03:53.327
I don't get how you can be my daughter.


00:03:53.494 --> 00:03:55.911
You always make me look foolish!


00:04:00.576 --> 00:04:01.451
It's...


00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:03.576
a blue planet.


00:04:04.035 --> 00:04:06.201
Earth, Planet Earth.


00:04:08.118 --> 00:04:11.075
-Are you sure?
-Yes, I saw it. I know where it is.


00:04:11.159 --> 00:04:13.075
You can't do anything.
That boy will finish you off!


00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:16.909
Fine. You want me to be proud of you?


00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:19.700
If you want to sit on this throne one day,


00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.660
there's your chance.


00:04:27.992 --> 00:04:30.867
Listen to me, Agata.
That boy is the ultimate weapon.


00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.617
I want him alive.


00:04:33.034 --> 00:04:35.741
When you capture him, I'll come for you.


00:04:35.824 --> 00:04:38.533
Yes, Dad.
It'll be soon, I won't let you down.


00:06:36.111 --> 00:06:37.819
LOPEZ GARAGE


00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:46.985
Here we go, the typical creep
on high beam from miles off.


00:06:47.152 --> 00:06:50.027
-Don't start, Juan. Let him pass.
-No, I will not.


00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:52.193
That hothead isn't overtaking me.


00:06:52.402 --> 00:06:54.776
And you'll ruin your timing belt!


00:06:54.942 --> 00:06:57.026
You clown! You...


00:07:10.484 --> 00:07:12.984
-Are you thinking what I'm thinking?
-Yes.


00:07:13.151 --> 00:07:14.734
What are you thinking?


00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:18.359
-I don't know right now. You?
-That wasn't a car.


00:07:31.066 --> 00:07:32.567
Jeez!


00:07:32.651 --> 00:07:35.900
I'll strip this heap
and make a pile on the parts!


00:07:36.441 --> 00:07:37.983
It's a meteorite, Juan.


00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:42.108
Or worse, an asteroid,
I don't really know the difference.


00:07:42.275 --> 00:07:44.525
Sorry, I'm getting nervous.


00:07:51.732 --> 00:07:53.440
Juan, I heard something.


00:07:53.524 --> 00:07:55.440
-Come here.
-You can hear something.


00:07:55.482 --> 00:07:58.981
-Maria, don't go near it.
-Someone's inside. Be quiet.


00:08:01.398 --> 00:08:03.815
Look, Juan! Look!


00:08:03.982 --> 00:08:07.565
-It's a gift from heaven.
-Like hell it's a gift!


00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.232
Look at the baby!


00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.898
We'll keep it.


00:08:12.064 --> 00:08:14.064
We can't, he's not ours!


00:08:14.231 --> 00:08:16.856
But look at him, he's lovely.


00:08:23.605 --> 00:08:26.647
Honey, that's no baby,
it's an adult dwarf.


00:08:27.897 --> 00:08:31.980
-We can't leave him here.
-That mustache is weird.


00:08:32.147 --> 00:08:35.398
-What do we know about kids?
-I know they don't fall from the sky.


00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:36.938
If it's a miracle, they do.


00:08:37.105 --> 00:08:39.563
I've been praying for months
for us to have a child.


00:08:40.355 --> 00:08:43.147
Maria, you're crazy.


00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:46.188
Hi, Daddy!


00:08:46.355 --> 00:08:48.313
Hi, Daddy!


00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.979
Look, Daddy.


00:08:51.437 --> 00:08:53.229
Look, little guy.


00:08:53.312 --> 00:08:55.271
He knows who his dad is.


00:08:57.687 --> 00:08:59.062
Little guy!


00:09:37.685 --> 00:09:41.810
Well, apart from the mustache,
he looks normal to me.


00:09:50.769 --> 00:09:51.934
-Good morning.
-Good morning.


00:09:52.101 --> 00:09:53.976
-My car's running wonky.
-Don't worry, my friend.


00:09:54.143 --> 00:09:57.518
We'll leave it like new,
we have the latest technology.


00:09:59.476 --> 00:10:01.476
I prefer more conventional
methods, thanks.


00:10:30.891 --> 00:10:33.016
Lopez! Push harder!


00:10:33.182 --> 00:10:36.974
You're a weakling!
Go, shithead! Harder!


00:10:37.099 --> 00:10:39.141
Wuss! Piece of shit!


00:10:54.932 --> 00:10:56.431
-Come on, here!
-Here!


00:10:56.556 --> 00:10:58.640
-Pass it to me!
-Kick it already!


00:10:58.806 --> 00:11:00.931
-You loser, kick it!
-Numbskull goalie!


00:11:01.098 --> 00:11:03.681
C'mon, mustache!


00:11:03.765 --> 00:11:06.556
Pass it, kid! Loser!


00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:09.972
Doofus!


00:11:10.139 --> 00:11:12.139
Pass it, you idiot!


00:11:27.305 --> 00:11:29.555
Goal!


00:11:30.639 --> 00:11:31.722
Give me five!


00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:35.179
-Goal!
-No way.


00:11:35.346 --> 00:11:36.929
I got a goal. What's wrong?


00:11:37.804 --> 00:11:39.138
Let's go!


00:11:39.971 --> 00:11:41.013
What's wrong?


00:11:42.929 --> 00:11:44.096
Ball hog.


00:11:45.555 --> 00:11:48.221
I told you not to do those things
in front of people.


00:11:48.429 --> 00:11:49.429
But I want to win!


00:11:49.554 --> 00:11:51.596
All you'll get is no one
wanting to play with you.


00:11:51.721 --> 00:11:53.304
That's the way of a cheat.


00:11:53.388 --> 00:11:55.221
A coward who won't play right.


00:11:55.304 --> 00:11:58.512
-It's how I play. That's me.
-Then hide it, son, hide it.


00:11:58.595 --> 00:12:01.012
Keep going and they'll think
you're a weirdo


00:12:01.178 --> 00:12:03.137
and you'll be lonelier
than the number one.


00:12:34.261 --> 00:12:36.218
Maybe you didn't tell them
the right time.


00:12:36.926 --> 00:12:39.593
-Are you sure you did?
-Sure I did.


00:12:39.676 --> 00:12:41.635
And the address?
Did you give them the address?


00:12:41.718 --> 00:12:44.510
-Is it on the invite?
-They didn't want to come, Dad.


00:12:44.968 --> 00:12:47.135
It's because I do weird stuff, huh?


00:12:47.301 --> 00:12:50.051
Not weird, honey, just special.


00:12:50.218 --> 00:12:52.426
Then why is it bad?


00:12:52.593 --> 00:12:54.218
Because you're in Spain.


00:12:54.426 --> 00:12:55.676
Look, son. Anywhere else,


00:12:55.843 --> 00:12:59.426
in Germany, France, Norway,
you'd be highly prized.


00:13:00.176 --> 00:13:02.884
The bad thing is that here,
tall poppies get cut down.


00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:04.467
If you stand out, they grind you down.


00:13:04.634 --> 00:13:06.675
Is that why my classmates didn't come?


00:13:06.842 --> 00:13:10.175
-Because I'm not like them?
-They'll never be like you.


00:13:10.342 --> 00:13:13.592
But if you don't do "your stuff",
you can be like them.


00:13:13.884 --> 00:13:16.716
Juanito, you don't need to
do anything special,


00:13:16.799 --> 00:13:18.966
nothing special, to go far.


00:13:19.133 --> 00:13:23.092
Listen, in this country, to be happy
you have to be mediocre.


00:13:23.342 --> 00:13:25.217
Come on, son, make a wish.


00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:27.549
To be normal.


00:13:31.716 --> 00:13:34.549
Juanito, next year
I'm making you a cupcake.


00:13:37.966 --> 00:13:41.423
20 YEARS LATER


00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:46.257
<i>...the best electrical appliances
at the best prices.</i>


00:13:46.507 --> 00:13:47.590
<i>Take the step.</i>


00:13:48.215 --> 00:13:51.423
<i>Naturally, with the guarantee
of Chip Technologies.</i>


00:13:56.590 --> 00:13:57.590
Yes?


00:13:58.882 --> 00:14:00.882
-Where are you?
-Uh... here.


00:14:00.965 --> 00:14:03.548
<i>-Where? Did you sleep in again?
-No, no.</i>


00:14:03.632 --> 00:14:06.506
In the office, doing the dispatches.


00:14:06.589 --> 00:14:10.422
-I went by before and didn't see you.
-I must've been in the bathroom.


00:14:10.589 --> 00:14:11.922
<i>-After, when?
-A while ago.</i>


00:14:12.047 --> 00:14:14.131
Yes, a while ago...


00:14:14.297 --> 00:14:15.339
I was in the bathroom.


00:14:16.256 --> 00:14:17.796
I'm coming to see you,
to tell you something.


00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:18.880
<i>-Okay?
-No, really,...</i>


00:14:19.046 --> 00:14:20.505
I'm tied up with the reports.


00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:23.756
-Wasn't it the dispatches?
-The ones that don't match the reports.


00:14:27.422 --> 00:14:28.089
Darn it.


00:14:53.879 --> 00:14:55.920
-Have you seen Lopez?
-No, I haven't.


00:14:56.004 --> 00:14:57.212
Neither have I.


00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:06.420
-You could've warned me, eh?
-Look out for the box!


00:15:19.211 --> 00:15:21.418
-When did you get here?
-I don't know.


00:15:21.585 --> 00:15:23.710
I came in early today, I'm so busy.


00:15:23.793 --> 00:15:26.543
Juan, you know I don't want you
to see me as a boss.


00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:28.503
You and I are friends above everything.


00:15:28.669 --> 00:15:31.128
-Does something smell weird?
-You're the weird one.


00:15:31.294 --> 00:15:33.543
It's cologne, expensive too.


00:15:33.627 --> 00:15:35.043
Since when do you use cologne?


00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:36.752
To discuss that,
I'll take off my boss hat


00:15:36.835 --> 00:15:40.127
and put on my friend hat.
Work and friendship can't mix.


00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:42.502
Technically, you're not my boss.


00:15:43.543 --> 00:15:45.917
She's starting today,
I hired her after all.


00:15:46.001 --> 00:15:48.417
-You got that girl the job?
-It's not like that.


00:15:48.584 --> 00:15:50.251
She deserved the job.


00:15:50.459 --> 00:15:53.751
Another thing is if something
came up in the interviews,


00:15:53.917 --> 00:15:55.251
a spark, you might say.


00:15:55.417 --> 00:15:57.167
You can't use interviews to score.


00:15:57.251 --> 00:16:00.251
Everyone knows that job interviews
are a bit like dates.


00:16:00.334 --> 00:16:01.834
No, they're not.


00:16:01.959 --> 00:16:05.709
On a date, what do you talk about?
Work, hobbies...


00:16:05.876 --> 00:16:08.001
Speaking of hobbies,


00:16:08.167 --> 00:16:11.458
you won't believe it, but ours
are the same: reading and travel.


00:16:11.541 --> 00:16:12.833
But everyone likes that!


00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:16.416
Help me plan something cool, as a welcome.


00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:18.000
We've never welcomed anyone.


00:16:18.083 --> 00:16:20.500
I'm putting on my friend hat to tell you


00:16:20.583 --> 00:16:22.875
that you and I haven't
been out partying in ages.


00:16:22.958 --> 00:16:25.415
Count me out. I'm getting breakfast.


00:16:26.415 --> 00:16:28.415
I knew it. You just got here!


00:16:31.833 --> 00:16:32.958
Darn it.


00:16:57.498 --> 00:16:58.289
Luisa?


00:17:10.623 --> 00:17:12.831
Good morning. Can you tell...


00:17:12.914 --> 00:17:14.455
No... Juan?


00:17:15.163 --> 00:17:17.163
-Luisa?
-What are you doing here?


00:17:17.913 --> 00:17:20.705
I knew in college that
you'd go far and look at you,


00:17:20.872 --> 00:17:21.872
a receptionist.


00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:25.122
No, I don't work here.


00:17:25.288 --> 00:17:27.621
I work in the company,
but in a real job.


00:17:28.787 --> 00:17:31.787
-Okay, you're kidding me.
-Amazing meeting like this!


00:17:31.954 --> 00:17:34.330
We must catch up.
But not now, I'm late.


00:17:34.497 --> 00:17:37.122
-Could you tell Jaime Gonzalez?
-Jaime?


00:17:37.288 --> 00:17:40.496
-You're going to work here?
-Looks like it. I still can't believe it.


00:17:40.662 --> 00:17:42.246
Did you have to do eight interviews too?


00:17:46.579 --> 00:17:47.871
<i>-Jaime.
-Yes?</i>


00:17:48.037 --> 00:17:50.037
<i>-Luis Lanas is here.
-Send her in.</i>


00:17:50.204 --> 00:17:51.246
Okay.


00:17:52.204 --> 00:17:53.703
You're great at it.


00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:56.453
You should seriously consider
being a receptionist.


00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:02.703
Normally with new people


00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:05.244
we have a welcoming party.


00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:08.495
A little drink. Are you into that?


00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:12.578
<i>Right, family, look out,
we're making an auto-selfie.</i>


00:18:12.745 --> 00:18:15.203
I know it's not a selfie,
strictly speaking,


00:18:15.411 --> 00:18:17.578
but you get my drift.


00:18:20.577 --> 00:18:22.494
A nice memento of your first day,
right, Luisa?


00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:25.327
That's what we're like here.
A great atmosphere.


00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:27.077
Going out and living it up
any day of the week.


00:18:27.244 --> 00:18:29.910
-Where's the bathroom?
-Through the door, on the right.


00:18:33.743 --> 00:18:36.034
-How do you know her?
-From college.


00:18:36.201 --> 00:18:38.285
-She was a friend's girlfriend.
-Did you like her?


00:18:38.452 --> 00:18:41.160
He wasn't a close friend...


00:18:41.285 --> 00:18:44.076
-I asked if you liked her.
-Jaime, no. I didn't.


00:18:44.243 --> 00:18:47.409
Sir, if there's nothing else,
we'll get going too.


00:18:47.993 --> 00:18:50.493
Stay here until I tell you, okay?


00:18:50.659 --> 00:18:53.201
Our shift ended two hours ago.


00:18:53.409 --> 00:18:55.409
Look. See that gadget?


00:18:55.825 --> 00:18:58.575
It's got more commitment
to the company than both of you.


00:19:00.533 --> 00:19:02.533
I always need my boss hat
with those two.


00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:05.867
We've had a drink.
That's enough, isn't it?


00:19:06.742 --> 00:19:10.033
If you all go at once,
she'll get suspicious.


00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:12.450
I want to order a pizza
with lots of black olives.


00:19:12.617 --> 00:19:13.825
She loves black olives.


00:19:13.908 --> 00:19:16.033
You asked in the interview
how she like her pizzas?


00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:19.075
When she comes back,
go to the corner shop for ice


00:19:19.242 --> 00:19:20.033
and don't come back.


00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:23.532
You know what that's called? Strategy.


00:19:23.699 --> 00:19:25.532
<i>The HR guy 's coming on to me.</i>


00:19:25.699 --> 00:19:28.157
<i>I told you he was already
in the interviews.</i>


00:19:28.574 --> 00:19:30.949
<i>I'll make some excuse and go.</i>


00:19:31.116 --> 00:19:34.406
<i>No, wait.
Remember Juan, from college?</i>


00:19:34.531 --> 00:19:36.406
<i>That's him, with the mustache.</i>


00:19:36.573 --> 00:19:38.073
<i>He works here too.</i>


00:19:38.781 --> 00:19:39.865
<i>Just as well he's at the party.</i>


00:19:43.491 --> 00:19:45.032
-Juan!
-What?


00:19:45.199 --> 00:19:48.448
-Yes, I'll stick around.
-Stick around?


00:19:50.365 --> 00:19:52.656
Juanito, go get some ice.


00:19:52.948 --> 00:19:55.865
We've been knocking it back so much
we run out of ice.


00:19:56.031 --> 00:19:57.073
Yes, there's ice.


00:19:57.823 --> 00:20:00.447
-No, there's no ice.
-Yes.


00:20:00.989 --> 00:20:01.780
Where?


00:20:16.405 --> 00:20:17.405
Ice.


00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:22.530
Where's Luisa?


00:20:23.405 --> 00:20:26.779
I don't want to brag,
but I think she got scared.


00:20:27.696 --> 00:20:30.571
The tension here was too much
for her and she chose to go.


00:20:31.071 --> 00:20:33.779
A shame, because I was already
thinking about my Aunt Clari.


00:20:33.946 --> 00:20:36.488
Don't give them that crap
about your Aunt Clari.


00:20:36.613 --> 00:20:39.778
Juan, they have a right
to know too. Don't be racist.


00:20:40.112 --> 00:20:43.403
A trick to keep going in bed,
and I don't mean sleeping.


00:20:43.778 --> 00:20:44.863
I think of three images:


00:20:45.029 --> 00:20:47.321
my Aunt Clari dancing,


00:20:47.488 --> 00:20:50.487
a leek pie and beige corduroy pants.


00:20:50.653 --> 00:20:51.570
Okay, got it?


00:20:51.737 --> 00:20:54.237
I go from one to another
in my head. One...


00:20:54.778 --> 00:20:55.737
the other...


00:20:56.612 --> 00:20:57.737
the other.


00:20:57.903 --> 00:21:00.153
That way I can spend
hours with a woman.


00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:02.861
Well, not hours, what a chore.


00:21:24.319 --> 00:21:25.902
Psst, Juan!


00:21:27.318 --> 00:21:28.235
What are you doing?


00:21:29.485 --> 00:21:32.318
-I was on my way home.
-Straight home or out?


00:21:33.776 --> 00:21:35.818
I don't know. Are you hungry?


00:21:36.651 --> 00:21:37.401
You?


00:21:38.943 --> 00:21:39.818
Pizza?


00:21:43.984 --> 00:21:45.067
Well, next time.


00:21:45.609 --> 00:21:47.859
-Hey, maybe I'll make it.
-You'll make it...


00:21:47.942 --> 00:21:51.610
-I will. What do you bet?
-You won't. See you tomorrow.


00:22:01.484 --> 00:22:02.734
Excuse me.


00:22:04.109 --> 00:22:06.108
Do you like black olives?


00:22:08.399 --> 00:22:10.774
-How's Rober?
-What Rober?


00:22:11.441 --> 00:22:14.566
-What other Rober would there be?
-From college?


00:22:14.733 --> 00:22:17.066
-Yes. Are you still together?
-Juan, please.


00:22:17.149 --> 00:22:18.732
We left college 10 years ago.


00:22:18.898 --> 00:22:21.316
We weren't even an item.
How could I be with Rober?


00:22:21.483 --> 00:22:23.608
I don't know, just asking.


00:22:23.774 --> 00:22:26.483
If he found out I was here
eating with you, he'd freak.


00:22:26.649 --> 00:22:30.149
-Freak? Why?
-Rober always, I don't know,


00:22:30.565 --> 00:22:33.565
-thought you were weird.
-People talk too much.


00:22:33.732 --> 00:22:36.440
He'd say: "Don't you think
he's hiding something?".


00:22:36.523 --> 00:22:39.773
I'd say: "Juan seems really normal to me".


00:22:40.315 --> 00:22:41.898
That's what I say.


00:22:42.773 --> 00:22:45.022
What do I have to hide?


00:22:47.397 --> 00:22:49.189
You wanted to know
if I have a boyfriend.


00:22:59.147 --> 00:23:02.647
-Let's go somewhere else, eh?
-We'll finish this and go.


00:23:05.314 --> 00:23:07.272
Will you keep it down?


00:23:09.271 --> 00:23:11.355
-What are you laughing at?
-Luisa...


00:23:11.688 --> 00:23:13.063
You, squirt.


00:23:13.771 --> 00:23:16.396
-What's so funny?
-Shut up, you old bat.


00:23:16.521 --> 00:23:18.813
Don't get mad, Luisa.


00:23:22.895 --> 00:23:23.813
What did you say?


00:23:23.980 --> 00:23:26.646
Luisa, we can finish up...


00:23:26.813 --> 00:23:29.688
-You gonna be the hero, or what?
-Me, no. I didn't say a thing.


00:23:29.855 --> 00:23:31.896
Maybe we'll bust your ass.


00:23:32.063 --> 00:23:33.854
-You, bust my ass?
-I didn't say it, it was her.


00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:36.979
-What if he does?
-It's illegal to hit a minor.


00:23:37.395 --> 00:23:39.520
-I'm 18. What's up?
-Jeez.


00:23:39.687 --> 00:23:42.312
It's illegal to hit people in general.


00:23:42.395 --> 00:23:43.979
See this finger?


00:23:44.145 --> 00:23:46.728
-I'll blow you down with my index finger.
-Two things.


00:23:46.811 --> 00:23:49.561
One, that's not your index finger,
it's your middle finger.


00:23:49.644 --> 00:23:51.603
And two, beyond that detail,


00:23:51.686 --> 00:23:53.603
you can't floor me


00:23:53.686 --> 00:23:55.854
with that finger or anything else.


00:24:01.394 --> 00:24:02.686
Here, the middle finger.


00:24:03.936 --> 00:24:05.103
<i>Loser!</i>


00:24:15.727 --> 00:24:18.310
<i>My son, remember these words,</i>


00:24:18.435 --> 00:24:20.518
<i>if you stand out, they'll grind you down.</i>


00:24:20.685 --> 00:24:23.685
<i>Tall poppies get cut down.</i>


00:24:23.852 --> 00:24:27.643
<i>Juanito, you don't need to
do anything special to go far.</i>


00:24:27.810 --> 00:24:29.643
<i>Don't get involved.</i>


00:24:29.810 --> 00:24:32.727
<i>No one gave you
any cards in this game.</i>


00:24:34.310 --> 00:24:37.392
FINAL DESTINATION
NEXT TRAIN:


00:24:47.976 --> 00:24:50.183
<i>107 to Central, please!</i>


00:24:50.391 --> 00:24:52.183
<i>107 to Central!</i>


00:24:52.391 --> 00:24:53.850
<i>Help, please!</i>


00:24:54.016 --> 00:24:56.141
<i>The breaks aren't responding!</i>


00:24:56.308 --> 00:24:58.141
<i>We're a runaway!</i>


00:24:58.809 --> 00:25:02.266
<i>107 to Central!
The brakes aren't responding!</i>


00:25:02.433 --> 00:25:04.100
<i>We're going to crash!</i>


00:25:04.183 --> 00:25:06.100
<i>We're going to crash!</i>


00:25:14.808 --> 00:25:17.140
What was that?


00:25:18.099 --> 00:25:20.099
IT'S TIME, TAKE THE STEP


00:25:22.807 --> 00:25:25.057
IT'S TIME, TAKE THE STEP


00:26:04.931 --> 00:26:07.638
Relax. It's all under control.


00:26:35.429 --> 00:26:36.346
What are you doing?


00:26:37.179 --> 00:26:38.637
I don't know!


00:28:47.215 --> 00:28:49.215
CHIT TECHNOLOGIES
WORLD HQ


00:28:49.381 --> 00:28:50.505
You're about to witness


00:28:50.589 --> 00:28:54.422
the birth
of a new technological revolution.


00:28:55.422 --> 00:28:59.505
I present a future member of our family:


00:28:59.964 --> 00:29:01.172
Chitobot.


00:29:02.713 --> 00:29:05.796
Your homes will never be
the same again.


00:29:05.963 --> 00:29:09.379
Ultimate cleaning:
it vacuums, sweeps and mops.


00:29:09.546 --> 00:29:13.672
Of course,
with the technical service of CHIT.


00:29:14.505 --> 00:29:16.213
It's time to take the step.


00:29:24.629 --> 00:29:25.379
Agata...


00:29:29.462 --> 00:29:30.462
We've found him.


00:29:30.628 --> 00:29:32.087
Are you sure?


00:29:32.253 --> 00:29:33.878
Someone stopped
a subway train in Spain.


00:29:42.877 --> 00:29:44.170
Hit the video!


00:29:46.878 --> 00:29:47.878
What video?


00:29:48.962 --> 00:29:51.545
Spain? What's someone like that
doing in Spain?


00:29:51.628 --> 00:29:53.711
Last night he stopped
one of our derailments.


00:29:53.877 --> 00:29:56.252
Did some idiot hit
the emergency brake?


00:29:56.377 --> 00:29:59.211
No, we always deactivate them
before causing an accident.


00:29:59.377 --> 00:30:01.002
We have the images
in the control room.


00:30:01.086 --> 00:30:02.169
I don't need them.


00:30:11.751 --> 00:30:13.043
None of them show his face?


00:30:13.210 --> 00:30:15.376
The whole planet is full
of our technology.


00:30:15.501 --> 00:30:17.752
-He has no way out.
-There's no time to lose.


00:30:17.919 --> 00:30:20.460
Warn my clones there
that I'm coming immediately.


00:30:20.626 --> 00:30:22.460
And stay alert.


00:30:23.001 --> 00:30:26.835
Remember, we're facing
the ultimate weapon.


00:30:28.960 --> 00:30:30.793
Coffee with cream and a croissant.


00:30:32.375 --> 00:30:35.125
The coffee and pastry no,
but I can cream you.


00:30:35.292 --> 00:30:37.375
Warm or hot?


00:30:38.834 --> 00:30:40.375
Sorry, sir.


00:30:45.499 --> 00:30:48.625
SUPERHERO?


00:30:48.792 --> 00:30:51.917
<i>Everyone's talking about
the strange subway event yesterday.</i>


00:30:52.084 --> 00:30:53.625
<i>An unknown man
leapt onto the tracks</i>


00:30:53.792 --> 00:30:56.209
<i>causing chaos and astonishment
among those present.</i>


00:30:56.374 --> 00:30:59.791
<i>We have exclusive images
from the security cameras...</i>


00:30:59.958 --> 00:31:02.666
He's got a comet on his back.
You can't go that fast!


00:31:02.874 --> 00:31:04.666
Let's do a bit of work, right?


00:31:04.833 --> 00:31:07.083
We get sidetracked by anything here.


00:31:07.249 --> 00:31:10.332
-You're right, it's no big deal.
-I didn't say that either.


00:31:10.582 --> 00:31:12.623
You stop a speeding subway train...


00:31:12.790 --> 00:31:15.415
-What?
-Explain last night, right now.


00:31:15.498 --> 00:31:17.415
-What happened last night?
-Don't pretend with me!


00:31:17.540 --> 00:31:19.958
-I didn't stop a train!
-What train?


00:31:20.041 --> 00:31:22.790
-What train?
-I'm talking about Jaime.


00:31:23.290 --> 00:31:25.290
-His weird party last night.
-Oh, okay.


00:31:25.457 --> 00:31:28.207
Look what he gave me today.
My personal cards.


00:31:28.290 --> 00:31:29.748
500 of them.


00:31:29.915 --> 00:31:31.415
I don't want to be dirty minded,


00:31:31.582 --> 00:31:33.332
but it's like he hired me to hit on me.


00:31:34.664 --> 00:31:37.581
Luisa, that's the way Jaime is.


00:31:37.747 --> 00:31:39.831
-What are you all looking at?
-It's nothing.


00:31:39.997 --> 00:31:41.539
-Let me see.
-It's nothing!


00:31:41.706 --> 00:31:42.831
-What is it?
-Luisa, it's nothing.


00:31:43.789 --> 00:31:45.664
Oh, that crap.


00:31:45.831 --> 00:31:48.538
You can see a mile off
that it's a publicity stunt.


00:31:48.705 --> 00:31:51.539
A guy with superpowers in Spain?


00:31:51.706 --> 00:31:52.914
Shut up, it's pathetic.


00:31:54.497 --> 00:31:56.456
-Not really pathetic, eh?
-Juan...


00:31:56.539 --> 00:31:59.996
A superhero turns up and he's Spanish,
the crappiest you can get.


00:32:00.163 --> 00:32:03.955
A superhero has to be American,
or English or Japanese.


00:32:04.080 --> 00:32:05.996
What, was he born
in Arguijuela de Todos los Santos,


00:32:06.163 --> 00:32:07.705
Province of Caceres? No, Juan.


00:32:07.788 --> 00:32:09.038
Luisa...


00:32:09.205 --> 00:32:10.830
imagine, not you and me, no,


00:32:10.913 --> 00:32:13.787
but if there were someone
totally altruistic,


00:32:13.954 --> 00:32:17.370
capable of risking his life
to save the lives of lots of people...


00:32:17.495 --> 00:32:20.745
No, Juan. Some things don't fit.
Superhero and Spanish, no.


00:32:20.912 --> 00:32:23.163
German, maybe.
He could be German.


00:32:23.371 --> 00:32:24.829
But Spanish?
Don't make me laugh.


00:32:24.995 --> 00:32:26.495
Who's the villain: Punctuality?


00:32:28.037 --> 00:32:30.579
Maybe he's not a superhero.


00:32:30.745 --> 00:32:33.579
-Maybe he's someone special.
-You're irritating today.


00:32:33.745 --> 00:32:35.745
Keep it up, and I won't
have dinner with you tonight.


00:32:36.412 --> 00:32:38.078
-Dinner, the two of us?
-What's wrong?


00:32:38.161 --> 00:32:42.244
-What are you talking about?
-Nothing, work.


00:32:42.411 --> 00:32:44.744
Then you haven't found out.


00:32:45.244 --> 00:32:47.578
Agata Muller has come to Spain.


00:32:48.661 --> 00:32:50.160
The vacuum cleaner lady?


00:32:50.368 --> 00:32:53.118
Well, the technological guru,
I like to call her.


00:32:53.577 --> 00:32:56.661
But yes,
basically she sells vacuum cleaners.


00:32:57.036 --> 00:32:58.619
You look nice today, Luisa.


00:32:58.703 --> 00:33:01.244
<i>News of the day is about
the visit to our country</i>


00:33:01.328 --> 00:33:04.535
<i>of possibly the world's
most famous businesswoman.</i>


00:33:04.910 --> 00:33:08.285
<i>Our people are already with
the multimillionaire Agata Muller,</i>


00:33:08.368 --> 00:33:12.035
<i>who's about to make a statement.
We go live.</i>


00:33:12.118 --> 00:33:13.910
<i>I've always wanted to meet
someone like this.</i>


00:33:13.993 --> 00:33:16.742
<i>We're used to pursuing
those who commit crimes.</i>


00:33:16.909 --> 00:33:18.742
<i>It's also important to find</i>


00:33:18.909 --> 00:33:21.076
<i>those who stand out
for doing things right.</i>


00:33:21.159 --> 00:33:23.409
<i>So I wish to send him this message.</i>


00:33:23.576 --> 00:33:25.409
<i>I know that he's listening.</i>


00:33:26.368 --> 00:33:27.743
<i>Whoever you are,</i>


00:33:27.910 --> 00:33:29.534
<i>I want you to know
that I've come to help you</i>


00:33:29.701 --> 00:33:32.409
<i>and thank you for being that hero.</i>


00:33:32.576 --> 00:33:36.576
<i>And to tell you that you and I
can do great things together.</i>


00:33:37.117 --> 00:33:39.367
Like I said, publicity.


00:33:41.533 --> 00:33:44.241
CHIT TECHNOLOGIES
BARCELONA OFFICE


00:33:44.325 --> 00:33:45.700
It's time to go home.


00:33:46.700 --> 00:33:48.575
It's time to go home.


00:33:54.865 --> 00:33:56.199
It's time to go home.


00:33:56.282 --> 00:34:00.366
<i>-First of all, good morning.
-Dad, it's me, Agata.</i>


00:34:00.408 --> 00:34:02.908
<i>Yeah, great. What do you want?</i>


00:34:03.783 --> 00:34:06.157
Jan's son, I've found him at last.


00:34:06.699 --> 00:34:09.240
<i>I didn't even think
you were still looking.</i>


00:34:09.407 --> 00:34:11.699
I told you I wouldn't let you down.


00:34:11.824 --> 00:34:15.074
<i>Yes, but it's been 30 years.
Don't expect me to applaud.</i>


00:34:15.782 --> 00:34:17.824
If you knew all the things
I've had to do...


00:34:18.656 --> 00:34:20.406
But now you can come and get me.


00:34:20.489 --> 00:34:23.698
<i>-Have you found him or got him?
-I'm very close.</i>


00:34:23.864 --> 00:34:26.448
He has no way out.
Only the easy part's left.


00:34:26.531 --> 00:34:28.948
<i>-Another 20 years?
-When you find out what I've done,</i>


00:34:29.114 --> 00:34:30.532
you'll be so proud of me.


00:34:30.615 --> 00:34:33.698
My technology has spread
to every corner of the planet


00:34:33.781 --> 00:34:35.114
and it controls everything.


00:34:35.198 --> 00:34:39.073
<i>Anyone else would've razed the planet
and been back in two days.</i>


00:34:39.156 --> 00:34:41.406
You said you wanted him alive.


00:34:41.781 --> 00:34:44.780
Come for me and we'll
raze the planet together.


00:34:44.863 --> 00:34:47.738
<i>If you don't have him
when I arrive, I will raze it...</i>


00:34:47.905 --> 00:34:49.530
<i>with you on it.</i>


00:34:58.446 --> 00:35:00.571
Gentleman, you have the big prize.


00:35:00.737 --> 00:35:02.530
So get on it immediately.


00:35:02.905 --> 00:35:03.905
Sure, boss.


00:35:04.072 --> 00:35:07.363
Still, we'll have to stop
the search the day after tomorrow,


00:35:07.405 --> 00:35:09.696
it's the patron saint's day festival.


00:35:11.946 --> 00:35:13.529
I'm the only patron here.


00:35:13.696 --> 00:35:16.821
And no one's stopping
until we trap Jan's son.


00:35:16.904 --> 00:35:18.112
-Understood?
-Yes.


00:35:23.486 --> 00:35:26.736
-Hi, Luisa. You're there already?
-Yes, half an hour ago.


00:35:26.820 --> 00:35:28.820
-I knew it.
-I'm on the bus.


00:35:28.903 --> 00:35:30.695
I'm 3, 4 minutes away.


00:35:30.778 --> 00:35:33.404
-For being late, you're buying.
-Okay.


00:35:39.153 --> 00:35:40.986
Relax, Dumbass. It's alright.


00:35:46.611 --> 00:35:49.694
<i>Jan's son, only you can hear me.</i>


00:35:49.777 --> 00:35:51.985
Please, can you turn the radio down?


00:35:52.152 --> 00:35:54.485
Radio? I don't have a radio.


00:35:57.902 --> 00:36:00.984
<i>If you can hear this,
you're who I'm looking for.</i>


00:36:01.151 --> 00:36:02.151
Who are you?


00:36:03.484 --> 00:36:05.777
-Me? I'm Pedro Luis.
-Don't get involved.


00:36:05.944 --> 00:36:07.069
Can't you see the state he's in?


00:36:07.194 --> 00:36:09.652
<i>Don't be scared. I'm your friend.</i>


00:36:09.735 --> 00:36:12.693
Please, could you stop the bus?
I need to get off here.


00:36:13.609 --> 00:36:16.734
Please, you're scaring the dog.
Can't you see?


00:36:17.193 --> 00:36:19.193
Driver, let him off, he's crazy!


00:36:19.276 --> 00:36:20.901
<i>I have to tell you two things.</i>


00:36:21.068 --> 00:36:24.109
God, turn it down,
my head's going to explode!


00:36:24.276 --> 00:36:27.900
<i>First, don't talk to me, I can't hear you.</i>


00:36:32.067 --> 00:36:33.358
Oh, forget it, forget it.


00:36:34.025 --> 00:36:36.984
<i>Second, you have to come see me.</i>


00:36:39.400 --> 00:36:41.067
<i>I am Agata Muller.</i>


00:36:42.067 --> 00:36:43.942
<i>Let's talk face to face.</i>


00:36:44.650 --> 00:36:47.192
<i>With your super-hearing
it'll be easy for you</i>


00:36:47.358 --> 00:36:49.567
<i>to detect the origin of my voice.</i>


00:36:49.733 --> 00:36:52.066
<i>You must have many questions.
But relax,</i>


00:36:52.232 --> 00:36:55.941
<i>-I'm here to explain everything.
-Just shut up!</i>


00:36:56.107 --> 00:36:59.357
<i>I don't get why it took you
so many years to take the step.</i>


00:36:59.399 --> 00:37:00.691
Yes, I'm coming!


00:37:00.857 --> 00:37:02.024
<i>You have nothing to fear.</i>


00:37:02.191 --> 00:37:04.856
<i>I know your secret
and I've come to help you.</i>


00:37:06.356 --> 00:37:08.481
<i>Welcome to Chit Technologies.</i>


00:37:11.899 --> 00:37:13.649
We were expecting you.


00:37:30.939 --> 00:37:32.272
Hello?


00:37:34.355 --> 00:37:36.689
Sorry, but I'm in kind of a hurry.


00:37:39.605 --> 00:37:42.105
You don't know how many years
I've waited for this moment.


00:37:43.439 --> 00:37:46.355
-You're the vacuum lady.
-30 years.


00:37:46.522 --> 00:37:48.189
A whole life hoping to find you.


00:37:48.355 --> 00:37:51.022
Sit down, please.
We have a lot to celebrate.


00:37:51.105 --> 00:37:53.646
What do we have to celebrate?
I don't know you at all.


00:37:53.813 --> 00:37:56.938
Well, I know you from the TV,
I've got one of your blenders.


00:37:57.021 --> 00:37:59.688
What you did in the subway
the other night was spectacular.


00:37:59.771 --> 00:38:01.063
Stop, stop...


00:38:01.229 --> 00:38:03.146
I had absolutely nothing to do


00:38:03.229 --> 00:38:04.729
with what happened in the subway.
Alright?


00:38:06.188 --> 00:38:07.853
You don't need to pretend with me.


00:38:08.020 --> 00:38:09.395
-I'm like you.
-Yeah, sure. Like me.


00:38:09.562 --> 00:38:12.646
A thou a month and on contract.
And you a millionaire. Just the same!


00:38:12.771 --> 00:38:13.896
We're from the same place.


00:38:13.979 --> 00:38:16.021
-From Masnou?
-Much farther.


00:38:16.188 --> 00:38:19.562
We can't spend all our lives on the planet
pretending we're like them.


00:38:19.812 --> 00:38:22.228
-Know what I mean?
-No. I don't.


00:38:22.395 --> 00:38:25.770
Say it like that and it's like
I was an alien.


00:38:26.228 --> 00:38:29.437
-That's just what I mean.
-Yeah, right, hilarious.


00:38:29.603 --> 00:38:31.353
When you get back to Planet X,


00:38:31.478 --> 00:38:34.811
give ET, Alf and Zoltar a hug for me.


00:38:34.977 --> 00:38:37.061
People can't melt things
with their eyes


00:38:37.227 --> 00:38:38.352
or run at that speed!


00:38:38.519 --> 00:38:40.894
People can't stop a subway train!


00:38:44.894 --> 00:38:47.894
Look, two things.
One, I don't do that stuff.


00:38:48.061 --> 00:38:50.102
And two, how do you know?


00:38:50.186 --> 00:38:53.186
I can take you to a place
where you can be normal.


00:38:53.352 --> 00:38:55.686
We'll go back home with my father.


00:38:55.811 --> 00:38:58.351
Yeah, sure, in a UFO. Right.


00:38:58.476 --> 00:39:00.393
I'm not the person you're after.


00:39:00.560 --> 00:39:02.560
-Besides, I'm late for dinner.
-Wait.


00:39:06.685 --> 00:39:07.893
That's why!


00:39:08.768 --> 00:39:11.142
You want to stay for her...
Who's that girl?


00:39:12.975 --> 00:39:13.975
You read my mind?


00:39:14.684 --> 00:39:17.143
I tried to convince you the easy way.


00:39:18.101 --> 00:39:20.185
-The easy way?
-You're staying here


00:39:20.268 --> 00:39:22.850
-until my father arrives.
-Get off!


00:39:23.267 --> 00:39:24.684
Get off!


00:39:29.684 --> 00:39:31.142
Man, look at my clothes!


00:39:37.349 --> 00:39:39.724
Sorry, but look what you did
to my clothes.


00:39:41.891 --> 00:39:45.141
I knew it. I knew you were Jan's son!


00:40:05.432 --> 00:40:06.682
What's all this about?


00:40:07.932 --> 00:40:08.973
Finish him off!


00:40:09.057 --> 00:40:11.390
Guys, this is a misunderstanding,
I was going to...


00:40:12.015 --> 00:40:12.847
Sorry.


00:40:16.972 --> 00:40:18.056
You dropped...


00:40:21.473 --> 00:40:22.182
Sorry.


00:40:56.430 --> 00:40:57.513
Agata, stop this!


00:41:05.095 --> 00:41:06.554
Stop this!


00:41:13.262 --> 00:41:14.845
-Get him, get him!
-Get him!


00:41:15.012 --> 00:41:16.928
-Where is he?
-Where is he?


00:41:18.011 --> 00:41:19.844
-There!
-Who's got him?


00:41:21.386 --> 00:41:22.554
He's escaping, that way!


00:41:23.012 --> 00:41:26.220
You can escape from here,
but not from who you are.


00:41:26.387 --> 00:41:28.554
And you stop bugging me
with that buzzing thing.


00:41:28.719 --> 00:41:30.178
It's really unpleasant.


00:41:48.218 --> 00:41:51.343
-We won't let him out of the building.
-It won't do any good.


00:41:51.510 --> 00:41:53.468
Besides, I know his weak spot now.


00:41:54.051 --> 00:41:57.677
Her name's Luisa Lanas.
I want her DNA.


00:42:29.967 --> 00:42:31.841
EXPLORING


00:42:33.050 --> 00:42:35.175
SAMPLE LOCATED
TYPE: DNA, SUBJECT: LUISA LANAS


00:42:40.175 --> 00:42:41.091
DNA ANALYSIS


00:43:17.006 --> 00:43:17.881
Shitty gadget!


00:43:22.755 --> 00:43:26.422
No, not a shitty gadget.
Small to medium appliance.


00:43:27.088 --> 00:43:29.589
Or as I like to say,
good old household goods.


00:43:29.964 --> 00:43:32.089
Hey, take it easy, okay!


00:43:35.713 --> 00:43:36.838
Bad goods!


00:43:37.713 --> 00:43:38.880
No, no, no.


00:43:39.255 --> 00:43:42.047
Okay, okay! No, no!


00:43:48.379 --> 00:43:49.379
Relax, eh?


00:43:52.379 --> 00:43:54.212
Whoa! Whoa!


00:44:00.336 --> 00:44:01.337
Back!


00:44:01.837 --> 00:44:04.087
Get back, you bug!


00:44:04.171 --> 00:44:06.921
Sit! Sit! Whoa!


00:44:08.212 --> 00:44:10.671
Hey, you! Come help me,
it's gone mad!


00:44:10.754 --> 00:44:11.879
This robot wants to kill me!


00:44:12.212 --> 00:44:13.628
Come on!


00:44:13.795 --> 00:44:15.670
What are you doing there?
Come and smash it!


00:44:16.628 --> 00:44:17.795
Come on!


00:44:20.920 --> 00:44:22.586
Hit it, go!


00:44:26.335 --> 00:44:27.377
Go on!


00:44:34.170 --> 00:44:37.336
Not a word of this to anyone.
Not the hug either.


00:44:48.710 --> 00:44:49.877
DNA SENT


00:44:56.501 --> 00:44:57.834
Come on, Luisa, answer!


00:44:58.001 --> 00:45:00.918
-Answer, please, answer.
-Juan.


00:45:03.459 --> 00:45:05.668
-Luisa, where were you?
-Where was I?


00:45:05.751 --> 00:45:08.334
Where were you?
Looking like that...


00:45:08.376 --> 00:45:10.376
I went to the restaurant,
but you weren't there.


00:45:10.543 --> 00:45:12.959
Sure, you wanted me
to be waiting another hour for you?


00:45:13.126 --> 00:45:15.001
If you didn't want dinner with me,
you could've said.


00:45:15.168 --> 00:45:16.583
Not want dinner with you?


00:45:16.750 --> 00:45:19.042
Of course I did, very much,


00:45:19.208 --> 00:45:21.125
but something crazy
happened to me.


00:45:21.208 --> 00:45:24.458
-Crazier than standing me up?
-Yes.


00:45:24.625 --> 00:45:28.000
-What?
-I don't quite know yet.


00:45:28.957 --> 00:45:29.999
Luisa, what are you doing?


00:45:31.082 --> 00:45:33.957
If I drink a bit more,
maybe I'll believe you.


00:45:34.916 --> 00:45:35.666
Look.


00:45:36.750 --> 00:45:38.042
-Jaime again.
-Don't answer it!


00:45:38.208 --> 00:45:39.417
-Why not?
-Just in case.


00:45:39.583 --> 00:45:41.250
-In case of what?
-Well...


00:45:42.457 --> 00:45:44.332
Shit, bad signal!


00:45:45.957 --> 00:45:47.874
This... Luisa, look...


00:45:48.041 --> 00:45:50.707
I know what I'm going
to tell you sounds weird,


00:45:50.874 --> 00:45:51.999
so I'll say it straight out.


00:45:52.916 --> 00:45:55.956
I just caught a smart
vacuum robot with 6 legs


00:45:56.123 --> 00:45:57.498
sending your DNA to someone.


00:45:57.581 --> 00:45:59.498
Please, when you hear
my message, call me,


00:45:59.581 --> 00:46:02.248
I'm coming over with this beast
so you'll believe me.


00:46:03.248 --> 00:46:05.373
I know your address
from your resume.


00:46:05.456 --> 00:46:07.330
I haven't seen any emails,
or Facebook or anything.


00:46:07.372 --> 00:46:10.081
Don't be suspicious of me,
like your friend Laurita86.


00:46:11.790 --> 00:46:12.790
Shit.


00:46:12.915 --> 00:46:14.831
-Go on, apologize.
-Really, Luisa.


00:46:14.915 --> 00:46:16.331
I'd love to tell you,


00:46:16.498 --> 00:46:18.790
but I need a few days to take it all in.


00:46:18.873 --> 00:46:20.830
If I say it straight out,
you'll think it's crazy.


00:46:20.997 --> 00:46:23.789
But not "crazy" crazy, no.
Crazy as in "sick".


00:46:23.872 --> 00:46:26.372
Okay, better tell me now
while I'm wasted.


00:46:26.455 --> 00:46:28.955
This wine cost a fortune
and I have to finish it.


00:46:29.039 --> 00:46:32.329
-Luisa, I can't tell you anything.
-Why?


00:46:32.454 --> 00:46:34.871
Because I have to go
and talk to my parents.


00:46:34.954 --> 00:46:35.788
-Your parents?
-Yes.


00:46:35.871 --> 00:46:37.663
-How old are you, 12?
-Yes. No.


00:46:37.829 --> 00:46:40.664
Cut the crap, Juan.
We both know what's going on.


00:46:40.914 --> 00:46:44.080
You know, I know, and so did Rober.


00:46:44.247 --> 00:46:46.788
Years have gone by,
but we still like each other.


00:46:46.954 --> 00:46:48.413
Always have.


00:46:48.579 --> 00:46:51.079
So cut the crap
and come up with me.


00:46:51.246 --> 00:46:54.329
If a girl like you
asks me to come upstairs,


00:46:54.371 --> 00:46:55.621
I'm up there like a buffalo.


00:46:55.746 --> 00:46:58.953
I would, but no one's
ever asked me before.


00:46:59.120 --> 00:47:01.245
But if I let something happen
between us tonight,


00:47:01.412 --> 00:47:03.620
it'd make me the worst person
in the world.


00:47:04.745 --> 00:47:06.537
What are you doing, leaving?


00:47:07.120 --> 00:47:08.995
Hey! Hey!


00:47:10.077 --> 00:47:11.953
Fine, then go.


00:47:12.120 --> 00:47:15.370
Go get your parents
to make you a cup of cocoa!


00:47:15.620 --> 00:47:18.537
What more do I need
to get a snog out of you?


00:47:19.162 --> 00:47:23.119
You're a little kid!
Go back to kindergarten, coward!


00:47:58.160 --> 00:47:59.951
I really am smashed.


00:48:08.492 --> 00:48:10.034
Where do you think
you're going with that?


00:48:11.784 --> 00:48:13.324
Hell of a technical service.


00:48:25.075 --> 00:48:28.199
What is it with you all
and that girl?


00:48:29.324 --> 00:48:30.533
She's not that great.


00:48:31.866 --> 00:48:34.324
If you help me, Luisa can be yours.


00:49:07.197 --> 00:49:10.239
I knew it.
When I saw the news, I knew it.


00:49:10.406 --> 00:49:11.572
Get inside.


00:49:12.156 --> 00:49:14.906
What did you want me to do?
Stand by with my arms crossed?


00:49:16.364 --> 00:49:18.906
I told your mother no,
you're not a dickhead.


00:49:18.989 --> 00:49:20.447
Okay, I got a bit overexcited.


00:49:20.614 --> 00:49:22.989
It's no big deal if I stop
a train every 30 years.


00:49:23.156 --> 00:49:25.072
No? You should've acted
like a normal person.


00:49:25.239 --> 00:49:26.906
But I'm not normal, Dad.


00:49:27.072 --> 00:49:28.989
-You and Mom knew that.
-Son!


00:49:29.155 --> 00:49:30.655
-What do you want?
-To know the truth.


00:49:30.738 --> 00:49:32.863
No, do you want fried eggs
and bacon for breakfast


00:49:33.030 --> 00:49:35.363
or pork scratching.
You look thin, son.


00:49:35.530 --> 00:49:38.238
I don't want anything. Well, one thing.


00:49:38.405 --> 00:49:41.321
I want you to answer
a very simple question.


00:49:41.488 --> 00:49:42.695
-Go on.
-Go on.


00:49:42.862 --> 00:49:45.695
Tell me, please,
that you're my parents.


00:49:50.070 --> 00:49:51.155
Don't shut me out!


00:49:51.238 --> 00:49:52.946
Speak up, the tension's choking me!


00:49:53.530 --> 00:49:55.529
Tension, no, it's the trip,
you're just tired.


00:49:55.612 --> 00:49:56.904
Come on, relax.


00:49:57.029 --> 00:49:59.404
Of course we're your parents.
What's this about?


00:49:59.570 --> 00:50:01.070
Let's talk about the day I was born.


00:50:01.154 --> 00:50:03.070
Mom, how long were you in labor?


00:50:04.695 --> 00:50:06.404
-I don't remember now.
-What are you saying?


00:50:06.570 --> 00:50:07.611
I'm an only child!


00:50:07.736 --> 00:50:09.528
Your mother and I don't have
the mind for such things,


00:50:09.694 --> 00:50:11.528
it was a long time ago.
What's wrong with you?


00:50:12.069 --> 00:50:13.444
I met someone.


00:50:13.611 --> 00:50:14.903
-A girl?
-No.


00:50:16.028 --> 00:50:18.486
Someone who told me
some very strange things.


00:50:18.653 --> 00:50:20.527
Well, a girl too,
but that's another issue.


00:50:20.860 --> 00:50:22.694
She told me she wants
to take me home.


00:50:23.361 --> 00:50:26.903
But not this home, no.
Way out to another galaxy!


00:50:26.986 --> 00:50:28.361
And don't say it's the weed,


00:50:28.444 --> 00:50:30.819
that was a long time ago
and not that much.


00:50:30.903 --> 00:50:34.777
So tell me, please,
if I'm from another galaxy or not.


00:50:37.110 --> 00:50:39.068
If you hadn't stopped that train...


00:50:39.485 --> 00:50:42.360
So, yes.
This is goddamn incredible!


00:50:42.443 --> 00:50:45.067
I'll tell you one thing.
I think it's terrible


00:50:45.151 --> 00:50:46.317
that you didn't tell me anything.


00:50:46.359 --> 00:50:48.151
Son, to me you're just like any other boy.


00:50:48.234 --> 00:50:50.901
Yes, but with one slight detail.
I'm an alien!


00:50:50.984 --> 00:50:52.776
Nobody needs to know.


00:50:52.859 --> 00:50:54.860
They tried to kidnap me, Dad!


00:50:55.027 --> 00:50:56.402
Who says they won't again?


00:50:56.485 --> 00:50:57.942
Now you do have to eat more,


00:50:58.026 --> 00:51:00.692
you're too thin to face
the forces of the universe.


00:51:00.859 --> 00:51:02.817
Maria, please.
Enough of the movie stuff.


00:51:04.317 --> 00:51:06.276
-It's time you saw it.
-Juan...


00:51:06.734 --> 00:51:10.941
-Juan, we said no, whatever happened.
-See what? You're scaring me.


00:51:15.525 --> 00:51:17.400
-Come here.
-Go in, son.


00:51:28.233 --> 00:51:29.733
Ready?


00:51:35.316 --> 00:51:37.857
Does it ring a bell?


00:51:37.940 --> 00:51:40.315
Tell me that's not what I think it is.


00:51:40.982 --> 00:51:43.357
You came inside this, son,
we don't know from where.


00:51:43.440 --> 00:51:46.107
This doesn't exactly come from Martorell.


00:51:46.190 --> 00:51:47.274
What did you want us to do?


00:51:47.357 --> 00:51:48.689
I wanted to call the police.
She was the one who...


00:51:48.856 --> 00:51:51.189
The police. Great, really.


00:51:51.356 --> 00:51:53.939
You're goddamn model parents.
Congratulations.


00:51:54.106 --> 00:51:55.648
-Thank you.
-Be quiet.


00:52:05.981 --> 00:52:06.856
<i>Hello, son.</i>


00:52:07.398 --> 00:52:09.064
<i>-Watch out.
-If you're watching this,</i>


00:52:09.148 --> 00:52:12.189
<i>things got complicated and
we had to send you far away from Chiton.</i>


00:52:12.356 --> 00:52:15.147
<i>But thanks to your extraordinary,
amazing abilities,</i>


00:52:15.313 --> 00:52:21.147
<i>I guess you activated this mechanism
at the age of 3 or 4.</i>


00:52:21.355 --> 00:52:23.063
Hey, I already had an inkling.


00:52:23.230 --> 00:52:27.521
<i>But this is hard to explain,
so I'll used these two puppets.</i>


00:52:27.687 --> 00:52:30.188
<i>This is Skorba. I'm Skorba!</i>


00:52:30.355 --> 00:52:34.105
<i>I'm very bad and have all of Chiton's
inhabitants under submission.</i>


00:52:34.272 --> 00:52:36.730
<i>And this is me, your father.</i>


00:52:36.897 --> 00:52:40.062
<i>I won't allow it! With my science
I'll create the perfect weapon</i>


00:52:40.229 --> 00:52:41.854
<i>to defeat you!</i>


00:52:41.979 --> 00:52:44.771
<i>I hope you're starting
to understand who you are.</i>


00:52:45.812 --> 00:52:47.479
Yes, I understand perfectly.


00:52:47.562 --> 00:52:49.604
<i>You won't defeat me
with any weapon!</i>


00:52:49.771 --> 00:52:52.311
<i>It's not any weapon,
it's the ultimate weapon.</i>


00:52:52.353 --> 00:52:56.020
<i>When my son is born,
wind will come from his mouth,</i>


00:52:56.103 --> 00:52:59.145
<i>fire from his eyes.
He'll be quick as a flash.</i>


00:52:59.311 --> 00:53:02.437
<i>And flying through the galaxy
he'll destroy your empire.</i>


00:53:02.604 --> 00:53:03.646
Did he say I'll fly?


00:53:03.812 --> 00:53:06.853
<i>Skorba will be looking for you.
Where did your son go?</i>


00:53:07.020 --> 00:53:08.811
<i>Left or right?</i>


00:53:09.311 --> 00:53:10.728
<i>Left, right.</i>


00:53:10.895 --> 00:53:12.311
Go on, tell him.


00:53:12.478 --> 00:53:16.561
<i>Son, this is an interactive hologram.
You have to answer: left or right.</i>


00:53:16.727 --> 00:53:19.810
Until you say which one,
the "phonogram" can't go on.


00:53:20.102 --> 00:53:22.810
<i>-The right.
-Good, you said right.</i>


00:53:22.977 --> 00:53:26.060
<i>That means you're too little
and didn't understand a thing.</i>


00:53:26.185 --> 00:53:29.726
<i>It's about misleading Skorba,
not giving yourself away.</i>


00:53:29.893 --> 00:53:31.851
<i>But never mind, you have to grow up</i>


00:53:32.018 --> 00:53:33.977
<i>to reach the intellectual level
of an adult.</i>


00:53:34.144 --> 00:53:36.352
<i>Don't worry,
one day you'll be ready.</i>


00:53:36.519 --> 00:53:38.852
<i>And when that day comes,
just get in the rocket</i>


00:53:39.019 --> 00:53:42.309
<i>and it'll take you back
to Chiton to save us, son.</i>


00:53:43.726 --> 00:53:45.601
<i>You're our only hope.</i>


00:53:50.726 --> 00:53:54.184
Well, this message must be
from ages ago.


00:53:54.351 --> 00:53:57.808
They must've found a way
to sort out their stuff.


00:53:58.933 --> 00:54:01.642
And not a word to anyone about this.


00:54:01.725 --> 00:54:04.518
Especially to Uncle Tonin,
three shots and he blabs everything.


00:54:04.684 --> 00:54:07.725
I'm not saying a word, but I think
they're waiting for you on that planet.


00:54:07.808 --> 00:54:10.767
Yeah, right, now the invasion
of this tyrant is my fault.


00:54:10.933 --> 00:54:13.808
They must've done something too.
I'd have to hear the other side.


00:54:13.933 --> 00:54:16.808
It's so easy to judge people
from other galaxies.


00:54:16.975 --> 00:54:18.392
Mom, leave that, don't touch anything!


00:54:18.517 --> 00:54:20.599
Finally a Lopez can do
something important.


00:54:20.766 --> 00:54:23.807
I once fixed Sito Pons's motorbike,
I know that's nothing, but...


00:54:23.932 --> 00:54:27.474
This month's very bad for me.
I'm doing the dispatches, the mortgage...


00:54:27.641 --> 00:54:30.141
Are they going to do
my quarterly sales tax for me?


00:54:30.224 --> 00:54:32.640
The oppressed citizens of Chiton,
Chiton, whatever it's called?


00:54:33.556 --> 00:54:35.974
-So every man for himself.
-No, son, no!


00:54:36.057 --> 00:54:37.974
They said you're their last hope.


00:54:38.141 --> 00:54:39.766
Yes, their last hope, my ass!


00:54:39.849 --> 00:54:40.807
Watch your mouth!


00:54:40.891 --> 00:54:43.766
How can I go to outer space
without insurance or anything?


00:54:43.932 --> 00:54:46.140
Besides, Dad, you always
told me not to stand out.


00:54:46.306 --> 00:54:48.306
Sure, but now we know who you are,


00:54:48.431 --> 00:54:50.140
you can't act like you're not who you are.


00:54:51.306 --> 00:54:53.681
First, talk properly,
you're unintelligible.


00:54:53.848 --> 00:54:55.348
And second, I'm outta here.


00:54:56.598 --> 00:54:59.097
Juanito, son. Just in case,
I'll make you a suit from this,


00:54:59.305 --> 00:55:02.305
-it looks like good fabric.
-I'm not putting on anything.


00:55:02.472 --> 00:55:05.264
A superhero can't go around
tearing ordinary clothes.


00:55:05.347 --> 00:55:08.806
-Superheroes don't exist!
-What do we know, son?


00:55:08.973 --> 00:55:10.639
Look. I'll just make it
and you can try it on.


00:55:10.805 --> 00:55:14.680
-I'm so excited...
-I'm not putting on any suit, period!


00:55:31.388 --> 00:55:33.554
Aren't you going to say anything?


00:55:33.763 --> 00:55:35.721
It looks so bad on you,
I can't even laugh.


00:55:35.804 --> 00:55:39.012
It's a nice, standard-issue supersuit.


00:55:39.095 --> 00:55:41.596
With a wig, he's a dead ringer
for the Queen of the Mardi Gras.


00:55:41.763 --> 00:55:44.971
-I'm taking it off, it's over.
-No, come here, hold on.


00:55:45.138 --> 00:55:47.888
Maybe if I put a bit of a dart here...


00:55:48.054 --> 00:55:50.970
-or some shoulder pads...
-No shoulder pads, no way!


00:55:51.053 --> 00:55:52.303
He looks like a junkie in a tracksuit.


00:55:52.345 --> 00:55:54.428
He just needs the flute,
the dog and the chocolate pastry.


00:55:54.512 --> 00:55:56.012
Look at Dad. Say something.


00:55:56.095 --> 00:55:58.387
A couple of washes will shrink it to fit.


00:55:58.553 --> 00:56:00.012
Besides, you're a growing boy.


00:56:00.095 --> 00:56:01.136
Yeah, a growing boy...


00:56:01.219 --> 00:56:04.011
Look, I copied this
from the supermen movies.


00:56:04.177 --> 00:56:07.427
If you get cold, put it here,
it makes a nice shawl.


00:56:07.594 --> 00:56:09.302
No, it's meant to be a cape.


00:56:09.469 --> 00:56:11.678
-It's for flying.
-So you can really fly?


00:56:12.387 --> 00:56:13.345
Apparently.


00:56:13.428 --> 00:56:15.677
That man from the spaceship
mentioned fire and flying.


00:56:16.552 --> 00:56:19.386
That man from the spaceship
is my father, he has a name.


00:56:19.511 --> 00:56:22.302
-What name?
-I don't know right now.


00:56:23.719 --> 00:56:26.551
I'm your father too,
my name's Juan Antonio Lopez


00:56:26.718 --> 00:56:28.593
and I'm telling you
you have to learn how to fly.


00:56:28.676 --> 00:56:31.468
You may need it one day,
you never know.


00:56:31.551 --> 00:56:34.301
Yeah, sure, learn how to fly.
How do you do that?


00:56:42.217 --> 00:56:44.468
Someone from town
is going to see me like this!


00:56:44.551 --> 00:56:47.718
C'mon, today's the day. Try to fly!


00:56:47.801 --> 00:56:50.301
Sure, try to fly. Like it was so easy!


00:56:50.385 --> 00:56:54.092
Flap like a magpie,
and watch out for the trees!


00:56:54.175 --> 00:56:56.675
-That's it, go on.
-Let him concentrate.


00:56:58.134 --> 00:56:59.592
Flap wider!


00:57:00.134 --> 00:57:03.634
-Like this.
-Not so bunched up. More!


00:57:04.300 --> 00:57:05.883
-There.
-Nothing.


00:57:06.008 --> 00:57:09.424
-What's he doing with his fist?
-That's it, there!


00:57:09.591 --> 00:57:10.674
-Try that!
-Go on!


00:57:13.008 --> 00:57:14.675
Nothing, it doesn't work.


00:57:14.759 --> 00:57:16.800
I think you'd better jump.


00:57:16.884 --> 00:57:19.383
Yeah, sure, jump.
I'll bust my goddamn head!


00:57:19.466 --> 00:57:21.216
Maybe this flying thing
is activated in the air.


00:57:21.299 --> 00:57:23.924
Trust in yourself
as we trust in you, son!


00:57:24.008 --> 00:57:25.966
-That's it.
-I know you'll fly!


00:57:26.174 --> 00:57:28.508
Move, that way.


00:57:45.756 --> 00:57:49.840
-God, he sure hit the dirt.
-Son, everything alright?


00:57:50.882 --> 00:57:53.048
Look how well you get up.


00:57:53.132 --> 00:57:54.882
-That's great.
-Does anything hurt?


00:57:57.339 --> 00:57:59.589
-It's my fault for listening to you.
-But son...


00:57:59.756 --> 00:58:01.339
-You'll get it next time.
-Yes, next time.


00:58:01.422 --> 00:58:02.672
Next time you jump off!


00:58:02.839 --> 00:58:05.631
No, I said there was
no basis to this.


00:58:05.797 --> 00:58:06.839
You're just a little imprecise.


00:58:07.006 --> 00:58:09.463
You need to get it right, that's all.


00:58:18.672 --> 00:58:20.796
Freak, you're a freak.


00:58:22.463 --> 00:58:25.755
Watch it, you're talking to
the hope of another galaxy.


00:58:25.838 --> 00:58:28.546
-The galaxy of the tacky, huh?
-You're wearing panties!


00:58:29.630 --> 00:58:31.630
They're not panties, you brat!


00:58:31.796 --> 00:58:33.045
Maybe I'll beat you up


00:58:33.129 --> 00:58:35.462
and you'll see who
the ultimate weapon is.


00:58:35.545 --> 00:58:39.337
-You gonna hit us with your handbag?
-Is the "S" for sissy?


00:58:39.754 --> 00:58:42.795
-Or subnormal.
-Or sausage-sucker.


00:58:49.336 --> 00:58:52.045
What? You're not laughing
so hard now, eh?


00:58:54.129 --> 00:58:55.587
-Run.
-Run, run!


00:59:01.336 --> 00:59:03.044
Holy guacamole!


00:59:03.961 --> 00:59:06.128
Juan, look! Look, Juan!


00:59:06.294 --> 00:59:08.878
-He's not flying, but he is levitating!
-Holy shit!


00:59:08.961 --> 00:59:10.628
-Saint Teresa!
-The Calcutta one?


00:59:10.793 --> 00:59:12.377
No, Avila. This is a miracle!


00:59:22.378 --> 00:59:25.210
-No way your saint does that.
-Where did he go?


00:59:58.876 --> 01:00:01.500
-Do you know where I am?
-Cala de Marbres.


01:00:01.791 --> 01:00:03.833
-Where?
-In Mallorca.


01:00:05.041 --> 01:00:06.416
Mallorca?


01:00:07.166 --> 01:00:09.416
Bucks' party got out of hand, eh?


01:00:22.415 --> 01:00:23.707
Damn!


01:00:42.164 --> 01:00:43.998
Look, you take Txatxarramendi road,


01:00:44.164 --> 01:00:45.289
past Legorreta and Kastelleta


01:00:45.414 --> 01:00:47.789
and at Amorebieta
you take the A-8 and straight on.


01:00:47.956 --> 01:00:50.664
Careful, if the first town
you see is Yiurreta,


01:00:50.831 --> 01:00:53.497
you're screwed, kid, you're in a jam.


01:00:53.663 --> 01:00:55.622
You turn the fuck around
back to Ibaneta,


01:00:55.788 --> 01:00:58.581
take the shortcut
from Goitzueta to Txoritokieta


01:00:58.748 --> 01:01:01.539
and then get the fucking A-8
just past Guantxoritzketa.


01:01:01.623 --> 01:01:03.289
A hell of a way around.


01:01:03.873 --> 01:01:05.997
Got it, or do I explain again?


01:01:06.663 --> 01:01:08.955
Yes, yes, absolutely clear.


01:01:14.747 --> 01:01:16.455
Holy crap!


01:02:03.036 --> 01:02:05.036
Mom, it's so obvious, this is ridiculous.


01:02:05.203 --> 01:02:07.703
-You don't notice the bump.
-No, not at all...


01:02:07.869 --> 01:02:10.285
And you can wear it all year,
it won't give you a hump.


01:02:10.452 --> 01:02:11.994
You'll see the sweat when spring comes.


01:02:12.077 --> 01:02:13.869
-No!
-Don't be tedious, son.


01:02:13.994 --> 01:02:15.619
If you get into a galactic tussle,


01:02:15.702 --> 01:02:18.077
just rip you clothes off like this,


01:02:18.160 --> 01:02:19.160
that's always imposing.


01:02:19.244 --> 01:02:21.201
Like I'd tear my clothes,
with what they cost.


01:02:21.368 --> 01:02:22.659
-No, I'm not wearing it.
-Listen, Juanito...


01:02:33.868 --> 01:02:36.284
-Does Juan live here?
-No.


01:02:36.326 --> 01:02:38.618
Are you sure?
Jaime told me he lives here.


01:02:39.034 --> 01:02:40.118
Luisa?


01:02:41.284 --> 01:02:42.201
What are you doing here?


01:02:43.326 --> 01:02:45.409
I found out everything.
How could I not come?


01:02:47.742 --> 01:02:51.033
-Relax, she's from this galaxy.
-Ah.


01:02:51.200 --> 01:02:52.325
Something to eat?


01:02:52.492 --> 01:02:54.992
-You're skin and bone.
-Mom, please.


01:02:55.075 --> 01:02:56.950
Forgive us, we're kind of nervous.


01:02:57.117 --> 01:02:59.366
It's the first time
Juan's brought a girl home.


01:03:00.116 --> 01:03:02.324
That's just the info we needed.


01:03:02.491 --> 01:03:04.617
I didn't mean you're an item, eh?


01:03:04.783 --> 01:03:06.575
-I didn't mean...
-Dad, please!


01:03:06.742 --> 01:03:09.617
We know what "being friends"
means these days.


01:03:10.450 --> 01:03:11.532
Like something cool?


01:03:11.699 --> 01:03:14.991
-Get them some lemonade, Maria.
-You get it.


01:03:15.157 --> 01:03:17.532
-Why didn't you tell me last night?
-I don't know.


01:03:17.616 --> 01:03:21.407
-I was afraid I'd look weird...
-But this is beautiful, Juan.


01:03:21.491 --> 01:03:25.448
-This is incredible.
-How did you find out...?


01:03:25.615 --> 01:03:28.906
Are you alright, Luisa? Your eye...


01:03:28.990 --> 01:03:29.990
-My eye?
-Your eye.


01:03:30.823 --> 01:03:34.615
It's the excitement.
I know everything and it's beautiful.


01:03:34.781 --> 01:03:37.490
They said they want to help you
get back to your true home.


01:03:37.573 --> 01:03:40.615
-You met the vacuum lady?
-Yes.


01:03:40.781 --> 01:03:43.073
She's really worried about you.


01:03:43.156 --> 01:03:45.781
Stop, maybe she didn't tell you
she tried to kidnap me.


01:03:45.865 --> 01:03:48.948
Yes. She's as nervous as you
about all this.


01:03:49.114 --> 01:03:51.239
About having found you and...


01:03:51.655 --> 01:03:55.072
she asked me to apologize to you
for being so brusque.


01:03:57.530 --> 01:03:59.197
What, don't you believe me?


01:03:59.280 --> 01:04:02.571
-I'm Luisa, why would I deceive you?
-Luisa, you're acting strange.


01:04:02.654 --> 01:04:04.196
-What about last night?
-Last night? What?


01:04:04.279 --> 01:04:05.446
-Yes, last night.
-Last night?


01:04:05.613 --> 01:04:06.279
-Last night.
-Yes?


01:04:06.363 --> 01:04:08.947
I think it's as important
or more than all this.


01:04:09.030 --> 01:04:10.822
Sure. Last night...


01:04:12.030 --> 01:04:13.405
lots of things happened.


01:04:13.697 --> 01:04:15.571
I don't know what you mean exactly.


01:04:15.738 --> 01:04:18.529
Ask him if it's more or less important
than betraying a friend.


01:04:18.613 --> 01:04:20.738
Ask him. Ask him!


01:04:20.821 --> 01:04:23.363
What's he saying?
What happened last night?


01:04:24.279 --> 01:04:27.195
-What happened?
-I know.


01:04:33.403 --> 01:04:35.903
No need to make a big issue
out of it, Juan.


01:04:36.070 --> 01:04:38.737
It was a couple of crappy kisses
in a doorway.


01:04:38.862 --> 01:04:40.695
Crappy? What's this about?


01:04:40.778 --> 01:04:43.612
Maybe you think snogging
in a doorway means we're an item.


01:04:43.695 --> 01:04:46.487
Now you're off to Raticulan
or whatever galaxy you're from.


01:04:46.570 --> 01:04:48.570
What do we do?
One weekend in your constellation


01:04:48.653 --> 01:04:49.820
and one in mine?


01:04:49.987 --> 01:04:51.862
No! You're a bad kisser,
let me say it again.


01:04:52.028 --> 01:04:53.902
But I'm telling you I don't want to go!


01:04:53.986 --> 01:04:56.027
Now I'm taking off
my possible girlfriend hat


01:04:56.111 --> 01:04:59.361
and putting on my
citizen-of-this-planet hat.


01:04:59.694 --> 01:05:02.694
Do you really think you can
keep living here, doing weird stuff?


01:05:02.777 --> 01:05:04.943
It's not weird, they're superpowers.


01:05:05.693 --> 01:05:07.276
Back it up a bit.


01:05:07.318 --> 01:05:09.818
Don't call them superpowers,
just super-sight and super-hearing.


01:05:09.901 --> 01:05:11.194
And X-rays in my eyes.


01:05:11.277 --> 01:05:13.736
Okay, you've got super-sight,
super-hearing and X-rays.


01:05:13.819 --> 01:05:16.569
-And I fly.
-You fly as well?


01:05:16.652 --> 01:05:18.860
-And super-strength.
-Well, you know what?


01:05:18.943 --> 01:05:20.485
Jaime has a superpower too.


01:05:20.610 --> 01:05:21.985
He's super-smart.


01:05:22.276 --> 01:05:25.443
And he figured us out because
it reeks from miles off.


01:05:25.610 --> 01:05:28.693
Or at least sensed it.
He's HR head for some reason.


01:05:28.776 --> 01:05:30.567
-Because he knows people.
-I know.


01:05:30.734 --> 01:05:34.025
Plus, he was your friend.
And you know he liked me a lot.


01:05:34.109 --> 01:05:36.150
And he has his clique, you might say.


01:05:36.234 --> 01:05:39.359
-Do you think I don't care?
-I didn't look like it in the doorway.


01:05:39.442 --> 01:05:41.400
Now you know what's going on with me,


01:05:41.484 --> 01:05:44.775
you'll understand that it's always
been hard for me to make friends.


01:05:45.609 --> 01:05:48.609
And Jaime always tells me
he's my boss and my friend.


01:05:48.984 --> 01:05:51.942
And well, technically
he's not my boss, but...


01:05:53.109 --> 01:05:54.609
he's always been my friend.


01:05:56.108 --> 01:05:57.816
And you're right, Luisa.


01:05:58.816 --> 01:06:00.399
I have to talk to him first.


01:06:00.983 --> 01:06:02.858
I love Jaime a lot.


01:06:04.358 --> 01:06:05.774
And he's my only friend.


01:06:16.441 --> 01:06:18.858
Don't you dare believe this shit.


01:06:22.398 --> 01:06:25.648
Very well. We'll get him my way.


01:06:33.315 --> 01:06:36.439
It seems you didn't understand
anything I said...


01:06:40.772 --> 01:06:42.522
Oh, you're into that, eh?


01:06:42.689 --> 01:06:44.939
I'm not much,
but I haven't really done it.


01:06:45.022 --> 01:06:48.064
But because I haven't tried it,
maybe if we do and it's cool...


01:06:49.939 --> 01:06:52.022
Juanito!


01:06:52.147 --> 01:06:53.564
Juanito!


01:06:53.731 --> 01:06:55.856
-Son, what happened?
-What's wrong?


01:06:56.314 --> 01:06:58.022
Oh, my boy. Are you alright?


01:06:58.106 --> 01:07:00.688
You argued? You're starting early!


01:07:09.646 --> 01:07:10.813
What's up with her?


01:07:14.604 --> 01:07:17.104
-That girl's no good for you.
-Out of the way.


01:07:18.521 --> 01:07:19.980
That's not a girl.


01:07:22.271 --> 01:07:23.271
See, Dad, it's not that easy!


01:07:23.313 --> 01:07:25.270
-Here, my nails are better.
-Get off!


01:07:25.354 --> 01:07:26.895
-Look at her!
-She's coming, go!


01:07:26.979 --> 01:07:28.104
Here comes the oddball.


01:07:28.187 --> 01:07:30.562
-Get your pants off.
-Pull that way.


01:07:30.645 --> 01:07:32.395
Stop, or I'll never learn
to do it by myself!


01:07:32.562 --> 01:07:34.729
Come on, son, show her who you are!


01:07:34.812 --> 01:07:36.187
-And who am I?
-I don't know!


01:07:36.270 --> 01:07:38.978
-Get your pants off!
-Pull!


01:07:39.144 --> 01:07:40.853
-She's coming!
-She's coming.


01:07:45.103 --> 01:07:48.019
Move, stay over there.
I'll take care of her.


01:08:36.351 --> 01:08:38.684
-Wait, wait.
-Maria, be careful.


01:08:38.851 --> 01:08:42.600
What did you do to my son?
Tart, oddball, bitch!


01:08:42.683 --> 01:08:44.516
Hurting my son?
Don't you touch him!


01:08:44.600 --> 01:08:45.891
Woman to woman, come on!


01:08:45.975 --> 01:08:47.350
Woman to woman!


01:08:50.308 --> 01:08:51.391
Let go of my wife!


01:08:51.558 --> 01:08:53.308
Don't bring my mother into this!


01:09:05.390 --> 01:09:09.432
Jaime, we're going to need
the real Luisa.


01:09:09.515 --> 01:09:12.932
No, no. I did my part.
You don't need me now.


01:09:13.015 --> 01:09:14.724
Besides, I'm going now,


01:09:14.890 --> 01:09:17.307
I remembered I left
my whites in the wash.


01:09:17.390 --> 01:09:20.098
Yes. By the way,
your washing machine's great.


01:09:20.264 --> 01:09:22.348
Totally reliable. Hats off.


01:09:22.931 --> 01:09:27.057
Jaime, you saw that
I can't bring him here by force.


01:09:27.140 --> 01:09:30.265
He has to come himself.
And for this I need bait.


01:09:30.931 --> 01:09:33.889
-Help me find the real one.
-That wasn't the deal.


01:09:33.973 --> 01:09:35.473
You're wrong.


01:09:35.639 --> 01:09:38.014
-You don't need me here.
-You're protecting him now?


01:09:38.556 --> 01:09:42.098
-You really believed that drivel?
-Of course I didn't!


01:09:42.264 --> 01:09:44.347
But it was kind of the truth.


01:09:45.972 --> 01:09:47.638
One moment...


01:09:49.388 --> 01:09:52.055
Juan, I forgive you. And I love you.


01:09:52.138 --> 01:09:54.305
How could I not forgive you?
You're my only friend too.


01:09:54.388 --> 01:09:56.221
But the main thing now
is that Luisa's in danger.


01:09:56.262 --> 01:09:57.680
Agata Muller wants to kidnap her!


01:09:57.763 --> 01:09:59.180
Yeah, it's wild. The lady on TV!


01:09:59.847 --> 01:10:03.722
Sorry... I think they're reading my mind.


01:10:19.471 --> 01:10:21.511
-You really think you can go now?
-Yes.


01:10:21.595 --> 01:10:23.720
-That wasn't a question.
-Ah, no.


01:10:24.970 --> 01:10:26.470
Oh, Jaime, Jaime, Jaime...


01:10:27.178 --> 01:10:30.471
I'm so sorry. This hurts me
more than it does you.


01:10:31.096 --> 01:10:34.303
No, actually I think
it'll hurt you a little more,


01:10:34.386 --> 01:10:35.428
unless you help.


01:10:36.595 --> 01:10:40.636
Agata! This isn't the way
to do things! Not like this!


01:10:41.261 --> 01:10:43.011
Do we have the trap ready?


01:10:44.261 --> 01:10:46.261
-It's almost ready.
-Almost ready is no good to me.


01:10:46.344 --> 01:10:48.094
My father's almost here.


01:10:48.719 --> 01:10:51.802
-So where's your real girlfriend?
-She's not my girlfriend! Cut it out!


01:10:51.885 --> 01:10:53.469
Call her what you like!


01:10:53.552 --> 01:10:56.802
-But she's in danger because of you.
-Thanks for the analysis, Mom.


01:10:56.969 --> 01:10:59.759
If you don't want to save
your planet, it's up to you.


01:10:59.843 --> 01:11:01.594
But at least save her.


01:11:13.884 --> 01:11:16.718
<i>-Hello?
-Luisa? Where are you?</i>


01:11:17.134 --> 01:11:19.051
Juan? I can barely hear you.


01:11:19.134 --> 01:11:20.968
Yes, well, it's the signal.


01:11:21.134 --> 01:11:23.468
-Where are you? I'll come get you.
-On my way home.


01:11:23.634 --> 01:11:26.008
-I can meet you there.
-No, no! Not your place!


01:11:26.092 --> 01:11:28.383
Stay where you are, there are people.


01:11:28.883 --> 01:11:31.092
-I'm at the Arco de Triunfo.
-Really?


01:11:31.258 --> 01:11:34.843
You won't believe it.
Me too! I'll be right there.


01:11:52.007 --> 01:11:53.174
Luisa?


01:11:53.341 --> 01:11:55.632
-What's up with you?
-Me? What's up with you?


01:11:55.716 --> 01:11:57.299
When did we meet?


01:11:57.466 --> 01:11:59.049
What's your favorite drink?


01:11:59.257 --> 01:12:01.007
Do you like black olives
on your pizzas?


01:12:01.174 --> 01:12:04.091
-Juan, you're being an idiot.
-Okay, you're Luisa. No doubt.


01:12:04.174 --> 01:12:05.757
Tell me what's going on.


01:12:05.924 --> 01:12:07.757
Luisa, I'm not normal.


01:12:07.841 --> 01:12:10.507
-I got that. You have some things...
-Some things, sure...


01:12:10.591 --> 01:12:13.716
Like I can melt ice with a look.


01:12:13.882 --> 01:12:16.506
Or I can see through walls.


01:12:16.673 --> 01:12:18.548
Or maybe I sneeze
and knock down a partition.


01:12:18.715 --> 01:12:21.090
Apart from all that,
yes, I'm run-of-the-mill.


01:12:21.173 --> 01:12:23.923
Fine. Is this when I laugh?


01:12:24.090 --> 01:12:26.090
I stopped the subway train.


01:12:26.256 --> 01:12:28.380
I can fly too,
but I found that out today.


01:12:28.964 --> 01:12:31.755
I've been given some dumb excuses
for dumping me,


01:12:31.839 --> 01:12:33.839
-but this is the worst.
-It's not an excuse!


01:12:34.005 --> 01:12:36.381
I'll tell you something.
We weren't even going out.


01:12:36.465 --> 01:12:38.590
-So there's no need to lie.
-It's not a lie!


01:12:38.756 --> 01:12:40.505
-I'm telling you the truth, Luisa.
-Please, Juan.


01:12:40.672 --> 01:12:43.089
All you left out is that you're an alien.


01:12:43.797 --> 01:12:45.089
What?


01:12:45.255 --> 01:12:46.630
Just what I needed.


01:12:46.797 --> 01:12:47.880
Don't go too far away.


01:12:47.964 --> 01:12:50.172
How about this:
If it's all true, show me!


01:12:50.255 --> 01:12:51.839
-Don't talk crap.
-Don't you say you can fly?


01:12:51.922 --> 01:12:53.921
-Then go on, fly. Do something.
-Yeah, fly...


01:12:54.004 --> 01:12:57.004
How can I fly here? They'll find us!


01:12:57.088 --> 01:12:58.713
-Who?
-Agata Muller!


01:12:59.004 --> 01:13:01.754
She's an alien too,
from the same planet.


01:13:01.921 --> 01:13:02.879
-Your planet?
-Chiton.


01:13:02.963 --> 01:13:04.171
What?


01:13:04.338 --> 01:13:05.379
If you make up a planet,


01:13:05.462 --> 01:13:07.796
don't make it sound like
a village outside of Albacete!


01:13:10.088 --> 01:13:11.421
What?


01:13:12.796 --> 01:13:14.879
-You made a suit and everything?
-My mother made it.


01:13:14.963 --> 01:13:16.838
You mother made you a suit to dump me?


01:13:18.670 --> 01:13:20.253
Really, Luisa. It's...


01:13:21.253 --> 01:13:23.337
You're making me do this...


01:13:24.503 --> 01:13:25.670
in front of everyone!


01:13:25.837 --> 01:13:28.753
But it's always the same with you.
Always the same!


01:13:29.337 --> 01:13:30.752
You're no help at all.


01:13:34.502 --> 01:13:37.252
See that? The Arco de Triunfo?


01:13:37.419 --> 01:13:40.253
I'll loop through it
and be right back.


01:13:43.087 --> 01:13:46.044
I've never been dumped
in such an original way before.


01:13:53.836 --> 01:13:56.751
Hey, smartass,
where do you think you're going?


01:13:56.918 --> 01:14:00.293
If you want to work
this area, pretty boy,


01:14:00.460 --> 01:14:03.418
you have to get permission
from Jeferson Noruega, like everyone!


01:14:03.585 --> 01:14:05.376
Sorry, I think there's been a mistake.


01:14:05.835 --> 01:14:07.626
-I'm the real thing.
-That's a lie.


01:14:08.543 --> 01:14:10.668
I know the real one: Osvaldo.


01:14:10.751 --> 01:14:13.085
And he does Robocop
Saturdays on Las Ramblas.


01:14:14.876 --> 01:14:16.835
We're all very confused.


01:14:17.001 --> 01:14:18.793
-This isn't a costume.
-Yeah, right.


01:14:18.960 --> 01:14:20.585
You're in your pajamas, man!


01:14:20.751 --> 01:14:23.459
Jef, we keep up the quality
so this dude can screw it up.


01:14:23.542 --> 01:14:24.667
You...


01:14:24.834 --> 01:14:26.875
Two things.
One, these are not pajamas.


01:14:26.959 --> 01:14:29.667
And two, I really save people.


01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:31.334
Luisa...


01:14:34.499 --> 01:14:35.249
Luisa?


01:14:39.249 --> 01:14:41.249
-Get in!
-Drive!


01:14:43.084 --> 01:14:44.250
Luisa!


01:14:44.542 --> 01:14:47.083
-Luisa!
-Wait a moment.


01:14:47.166 --> 01:14:49.249
You're not leaving
until you tell us where you got it.


01:14:49.291 --> 01:14:52.041
-I don't want any trouble, okay?
-Oh, no?


01:14:59.540 --> 01:15:01.582
<i>It's me again, son of Jan.</i>


01:15:01.748 --> 01:15:05.332
<i>I don't want to hurt Luisa,
so don't make me waste my time.</i>


01:15:05.415 --> 01:15:07.707
-Don't you dare!
-No?


01:15:08.582 --> 01:15:10.957
Get outta here, you clown!


01:15:11.040 --> 01:15:13.664
-What do you want from me?
-Get outta here!


01:15:21.623 --> 01:15:22.873
The sword!


01:15:24.581 --> 01:15:26.956
<i>Accept it, you're not the others.</i>


01:15:28.872 --> 01:15:30.497
-Fuck, you idiot!
-Sorry, man!


01:15:30.581 --> 01:15:32.997
-You tore my suit!
-It was already torn.


01:15:33.081 --> 01:15:34.247
Like hell it was!


01:15:35.372 --> 01:15:36.664
<i>My father will be here soon.</i>


01:15:36.747 --> 01:15:40.580
<i>Join us and together we'll rule
these pathetic creatures.</i>


01:15:47.789 --> 01:15:49.830
<i>-I'll wait for you here.
-Where are you?</i>


01:15:49.996 --> 01:15:52.996
<i>-Where's Luisa?
-You know where to find me.</i>


01:16:25.370 --> 01:16:27.245
Excuse me, Agata Muller's office?


01:16:55.660 --> 01:16:56.868
-Juan, help us!
-Where were you?


01:16:57.035 --> 01:16:59.243
-Help us, look at us!
-Get us out of here!


01:16:59.368 --> 01:17:00.785
-Use your power!
-And tell me what's happening!


01:17:00.952 --> 01:17:03.410
-Careful, it's a trap.
-Where were you?


01:17:03.493 --> 01:17:06.534
If you speak at the same time,
I can't understand you.


01:17:06.617 --> 01:17:08.409
Don't get out of the elevator,
it's a trap.


01:17:13.242 --> 01:17:15.576
-Juan, what's going on?
-I told you, Luisa.


01:17:15.701 --> 01:17:17.034
He has powers, I've seen it!


01:17:17.117 --> 01:17:20.408
-People don't have 'powers'.
-Juanito, she doesn't believe it.


01:17:20.575 --> 01:17:22.117
-Go on, fly.
-How can I fly?


01:17:22.284 --> 01:17:24.451
We're inside. I'll bang myself silly!


01:17:24.534 --> 01:17:27.701
-Then super-strength or super-vision.
-It's super-sight!


01:17:27.784 --> 01:17:29.951
Supervision is something else,
that's supervising!


01:17:30.034 --> 01:17:32.616
You don't have to correct me
in front of her, eh, Juanito?


01:17:32.700 --> 01:17:34.241
You guys are terrible!


01:17:35.908 --> 01:17:36.991
Your underwear.


01:17:39.116 --> 01:17:40.783
You're wearing a black bra...


01:17:41.116 --> 01:17:42.700
with a bit of padding.


01:17:43.408 --> 01:17:46.949
You actually wear panties...
and they're from another set.


01:17:49.990 --> 01:17:53.491
-You have a tattoo?
-Wow, that's hot.


01:17:53.575 --> 01:17:54.866
It says 'Rober'?


01:17:55.866 --> 01:17:57.824
Didn't you tell me
you were half going out?


01:17:57.907 --> 01:18:01.657
-Don't talk about Rober now!
-I see something too.


01:18:01.824 --> 01:18:05.282
Yes, you have a mole.
Just there, above the...


01:18:05.365 --> 01:18:08.074
You don't see a thing! And untie me!


01:18:09.239 --> 01:18:10.031
Juan!


01:18:10.698 --> 01:18:12.073
What's wrong with you?


01:18:12.698 --> 01:18:13.489
Juan!


01:18:14.031 --> 01:18:15.448
<i>-I hear a noise.
-What noise?</i>


01:18:15.531 --> 01:18:17.489
<i>-A noise.
-Suffer, suffer...</i>


01:18:21.073 --> 01:18:22.155
The noise!


01:18:25.906 --> 01:18:27.239
It must be the speakers.


01:18:27.406 --> 01:18:29.073
Luisa, we have to buck him up
so he gets strong.


01:18:29.864 --> 01:18:31.323
Juan, I forgive you.


01:18:31.406 --> 01:18:33.073
I know you were after Luisa,
but I'm getting over it.


01:18:33.156 --> 01:18:34.988
Why bring that up now?


01:18:35.072 --> 01:18:36.655
-So you wangled me the job.
-Luisa,


01:18:36.738 --> 01:18:38.822
are we doing what
we're doing or not here?


01:18:39.947 --> 01:18:43.238
Tell him you like him too.
You'd tattoo his name on your thigh.


01:18:44.572 --> 01:18:46.363
I'm serious! Say something nice!


01:18:47.029 --> 01:18:48.946
Juan, this...


01:18:50.946 --> 01:18:52.071
You're, you're...


01:18:55.321 --> 01:18:56.280
really sweet.


01:18:58.238 --> 01:19:00.362
What's that shit?
You almost finished him off!


01:19:00.529 --> 01:19:04.737
-Tell him something epic!
-Yes, yes... Juan, when...


01:19:04.904 --> 01:19:08.029
When I said a Spanish superhero
was pathetic,


01:19:08.112 --> 01:19:09.571
it's because I didn't know
that you were one.


01:19:09.821 --> 01:19:11.654
Actually, I still think it's pathetic.


01:19:11.821 --> 01:19:14.986
As for the suit, don't worry,
we'll do something about it, alright?


01:19:15.070 --> 01:19:17.653
So gather strength from somewhere
and get us out of here now!


01:19:19.903 --> 01:19:22.695
It's not working.
It never fails in the movies.


01:19:23.070 --> 01:19:24.403
What a shitty superhero!


01:19:26.360 --> 01:19:27.402
-What did you say?
-Sorry,


01:19:27.569 --> 01:19:29.611
but look what he's like
with just some buzzing.


01:19:31.986 --> 01:19:34.653
-No, repeat what you said.
-What a shitty superhero!


01:19:34.778 --> 01:19:36.903
Look at him lying there. Pathetic!


01:19:37.070 --> 01:19:39.444
-You failure.
-Insult him more.


01:19:40.110 --> 01:19:42.402
Shitty superhero!


01:19:45.027 --> 01:19:46.152
It's working.


01:19:46.319 --> 01:19:47.735
Insulting him works.


01:19:47.819 --> 01:19:50.109
CAMERA 25 EXT. TOWER


01:20:00.027 --> 01:20:01.819
It's time to go home.


01:20:07.693 --> 01:20:09.026
-Loser!
-Useless!


01:20:09.109 --> 01:20:12.068
Superhero, sure.
Supershithead, that's you!


01:20:12.151 --> 01:20:13.693
-Idiot!
-Incompetent!


01:20:13.859 --> 01:20:17.233
-Unpunctual!
-You're a flop, a mediocre superhero!


01:20:17.275 --> 01:20:19.733
You're embarrassing to me. Second rate!


01:20:19.817 --> 01:20:25.525
Your English is crap, intermediate level.
And your Powerpoint is awful!


01:20:25.608 --> 01:20:28.024
-You kiss real shitty!
-Really?


01:20:28.482 --> 01:20:29.232
I knew it.


01:20:29.274 --> 01:20:31.525
How could he kiss right
with that cop mustache?


01:20:48.274 --> 01:20:49.066
Dad!


01:20:49.566 --> 01:20:52.857
-First of all, good morning.
-I was looking forward to seeing you.


01:20:53.024 --> 01:20:55.231
And I'm looking forward
to seeing Jan's son!


01:20:56.940 --> 01:20:59.648
-He's in my power.
-Let's see if that's true.


01:21:04.649 --> 01:21:06.481
You're making a fool of yourself.


01:21:06.648 --> 01:21:10.065
Not any fool, no.
The biggest fool in the galaxy!


01:21:10.231 --> 01:21:11.981
These people know lots of planets.


01:21:12.065 --> 01:21:14.481
They'll laugh at you
in all of the constellations.


01:21:14.565 --> 01:21:17.315
You know where Andromeda is?
Well, way beyond that,


01:21:17.398 --> 01:21:19.480
they'll laugh at how pathetic you are!


01:21:57.395 --> 01:22:01.187
If you can fly, I don't get
why you're late for work every day.


01:22:02.062 --> 01:22:04.145
Now you know I'm a superhero,


01:22:04.312 --> 01:22:06.688
don't tell anyone at the office.
Some people really gossip.


01:22:06.771 --> 01:22:08.729
Well, you being a superhero,
we'll see about that.


01:22:08.896 --> 01:22:11.228
-Shall I let go of you?
-No, no!


01:22:11.270 --> 01:22:12.228
-I believe you.
-Alright.


01:22:12.353 --> 01:22:13.687
Where do we go now?


01:22:13.853 --> 01:22:16.270
Where all 30-year-olds go
when they're in a spot.


01:22:18.812 --> 01:22:21.562
No, no... It can't be!


01:22:21.645 --> 01:22:23.561
He can't have done this.


01:22:24.811 --> 01:22:27.269
-Dad...
-I want to make one thing clear.


01:22:27.352 --> 01:22:30.102
Not for a moment did I believe
that you'd found him.


01:22:31.061 --> 01:22:32.352
He was here.


01:22:33.352 --> 01:22:38.811
I look at you and I want to push
the button and send all this to shit!


01:22:41.561 --> 01:22:43.977
You're a shame to your family.


01:22:44.436 --> 01:22:48.435
At your age, your grandma Ursula
had already subjugated a whole galaxy!


01:22:48.768 --> 01:22:51.351
Your cousin Virguis is just 18


01:22:51.435 --> 01:22:54.393
and he's already done two genocides
on Alpha Centauri!


01:22:54.560 --> 01:22:56.226
And look at you!


01:22:56.310 --> 01:22:58.893
How have you let
this planet go on like this?


01:22:59.268 --> 01:23:02.809
Alive! So alive it's disgusting!


01:23:03.600 --> 01:23:06.725
Where's the lava, the chaos!


01:23:06.892 --> 01:23:09.350
I want volcanoes everywhere!


01:23:10.560 --> 01:23:14.850
The whole planet's under my control,
although they don't know it.


01:23:15.017 --> 01:23:17.225
What good is it
if they don't know it?


01:23:17.892 --> 01:23:20.475
You're like a useless pet, like a...


01:23:20.725 --> 01:23:25.224
I don't know what you are, Agata,
but I wish you weren't my daughter!


01:23:25.683 --> 01:23:28.558
Where's your mettle
to be leader of Chiton?


01:23:28.724 --> 01:23:30.516
Where's your character?


01:23:30.683 --> 01:23:34.308
Where's your mettle
to do important things?


01:23:35.349 --> 01:23:36.808
Right here.


01:23:52.390 --> 01:23:53.848
<i>At last, my girl.</i>


01:23:54.807 --> 01:23:58.390
<i>Now, yes. I am proud of you.</i>


01:24:17.806 --> 01:24:19.056
Any objections?


01:24:20.556 --> 01:24:24.431
Then move it.
I have a planet to raze.


01:24:28.971 --> 01:24:30.888
-Are you sure?
-Look, Luisa.


01:24:31.055 --> 01:24:32.846
I may have all the superpowers,


01:24:32.930 --> 01:24:34.430
but understanding you
isn't one of them yet.


01:24:34.596 --> 01:24:35.555
-Me?
-Yes, you.


01:24:35.721 --> 01:24:36.721
A few days ago,


01:24:36.888 --> 01:24:38.721
you thought being a superhero
was pathetic.


01:24:38.888 --> 01:24:40.221
Now you won't burn
the suit, just in case.


01:24:40.305 --> 01:24:43.095
Agata will keep looking for you
and you'll need to defend yourself.


01:24:43.262 --> 01:24:45.805
If I stop being a superhero,
maybe she'll stop looking.


01:24:46.596 --> 01:24:48.555
I shouldn't have stopped
that darn subway train.


01:24:48.721 --> 01:24:50.221
-That's when the problems started.
-Oh, really?


01:24:50.346 --> 01:24:52.846
Were you really doing
so great before this?


01:24:53.388 --> 01:24:54.929
Burning the suit
won't make you normal.


01:24:55.012 --> 01:24:57.054
You know what really makes me mad?


01:24:57.220 --> 01:24:59.762
Precisely these days
I couldn't be normal.


01:25:00.137 --> 01:25:02.054
If I had been,
we wouldn't be arguing now.


01:25:02.220 --> 01:25:04.304
Or we'd be arguing over
whether to go out to dinner or not.


01:25:04.470 --> 01:25:07.678
Or if we'd meet up again,
which, by the way, I want to.


01:25:09.719 --> 01:25:11.844
But you can't choose
to be like everyone else


01:25:11.928 --> 01:25:13.386
because you're not like everyone else.


01:25:15.844 --> 01:25:18.220
I can choose. Look.


01:25:24.719 --> 01:25:26.344
Tell them this is going to stick.


01:25:26.428 --> 01:25:28.219
Give them some time,
I know Juan.


01:25:28.261 --> 01:25:31.428
You're his parents,
but I'm his boss and his friend.


01:25:31.593 --> 01:25:34.760
And you're not his parents, parents.
So listen to me.


01:25:36.552 --> 01:25:38.177
I saw this coming!


01:25:38.218 --> 01:25:40.635
-Tell Juanito to hide!
-What are you doing, Juan?


01:25:40.802 --> 01:25:42.593
These scum will see who his father is!


01:25:42.677 --> 01:25:44.717
When I find the cartridges,
I'll show 'em.


01:25:45.259 --> 01:25:46.759
What's going on here?


01:25:47.801 --> 01:25:49.010
That's going on.


01:25:55.677 --> 01:25:57.051
-It's not burning!
-Yes it is.


01:25:57.217 --> 01:25:58.801
It just needs to catch fire.


01:25:58.967 --> 01:26:00.092
Of course it'll burn.


01:26:00.259 --> 01:26:02.259
It wouldn't be the weirdest thing
we've seen lately.


01:26:02.342 --> 01:26:04.884
Now everything that happens here
has to be weird!


01:26:05.051 --> 01:26:06.717
Let's stop being so paranoid.


01:26:06.884 --> 01:26:08.384
Juanito!


01:26:08.551 --> 01:26:12.216
Juanito, look!
The aliens are invading!


01:26:27.633 --> 01:26:29.800
She couldn't be
a bigger pain in the ass.


01:26:29.966 --> 01:26:31.883
What's the suit doing there?


01:26:31.966 --> 01:26:34.466
-I'm not wearing it anymore, Mom!
-Why not?


01:26:34.633 --> 01:26:37.257
It turned out so nice,
and the stitching I had to do!


01:26:37.924 --> 01:26:39.715
How can you be so tiresome?


01:26:39.799 --> 01:26:42.757
Where are going with a UFO
right here in town?


01:26:42.840 --> 01:26:46.549
You must be really dumb.
I don't want any trouble!


01:26:46.715 --> 01:26:50.089
-First of all, good morning.
-I'm not going to your planet!


01:26:50.256 --> 01:26:52.840
-You didn't persuade me!
-I don't have to persuade you.


01:26:52.965 --> 01:26:56.090
I'm going to raze this planet,
starting with your family.


01:26:56.174 --> 01:26:58.924
Now you're razing the planet.
With what, a giant toaster?


01:26:59.090 --> 01:27:01.006
Have you looked at yourself?


01:27:27.838 --> 01:27:29.255
The suit!


01:27:29.422 --> 01:27:31.213
-The suit!
-The suit!


01:27:33.047 --> 01:27:34.463
-Come on.
-The stick!


01:27:37.962 --> 01:27:38.962
-Be careful.
-Here, Juan.


01:27:39.129 --> 01:27:40.129
-Come on!
-Come here.


01:27:40.296 --> 01:27:42.421
-Tell me you're not scared.
-I'm not scared!


01:27:42.504 --> 01:27:43.421
Even you don't believe that.


01:27:43.504 --> 01:27:46.254
Jaime, if she tells me not
to be scared, I say I'm not.


01:27:46.337 --> 01:27:48.212
But sure I'm scared.
Look at that monstrosity!


01:27:48.379 --> 01:27:51.836
-Two days in the same underpants!
-It keeps growing!


01:27:53.545 --> 01:27:54.253
Come on.


01:27:55.128 --> 01:27:56.671
-It's hot, it's hot!
-Alright...


01:27:56.837 --> 01:27:59.296
Put a foot in here, in here!


01:28:04.420 --> 01:28:07.336
If my mom helps me put on
the suit, I'll never have charisma.


01:28:07.503 --> 01:28:09.211
It's almost on us, Juan!


01:28:11.878 --> 01:28:13.045
Go!


01:28:16.002 --> 01:28:17.044
Leave me alone with her!


01:28:17.210 --> 01:28:19.002
-How can we go?
-Get out of here!


01:28:19.210 --> 01:28:21.460
Go! Go!


01:28:31.794 --> 01:28:33.294
What?


01:28:33.544 --> 01:28:35.127
Whatever you say, he's my son.


01:28:38.794 --> 01:28:40.502
By the Great Hornspoon!


01:28:41.251 --> 01:28:42.834
Leave my family alone!


01:28:43.001 --> 01:28:45.834
-This is between you and me!
-Family...


01:28:46.001 --> 01:28:47.793
Family is overrated.


01:28:57.583 --> 01:28:59.334
My shotgun!


01:29:03.834 --> 01:29:05.793
-Hold on, Dad!
-I can't, son!


01:29:05.959 --> 01:29:07.708
It looks like I can't!


01:29:07.792 --> 01:29:10.042
Hold on, Juan! Hold on!


01:29:14.208 --> 01:29:15.833
I'm sorry.


01:29:16.000 --> 01:29:19.207
-I think it's time to stand out!
-Of course, son!


01:29:19.249 --> 01:29:22.124
Show the universe
what the Lopezes are worth!


01:29:25.624 --> 01:29:26.624
Dad!


01:29:29.582 --> 01:29:33.457
Relax, son!
I've got it all under control!


01:29:34.999 --> 01:29:36.041
He's been sucked up!


01:29:50.206 --> 01:29:52.665
-Isn't that the loser?
-Be quiet.


01:30:03.706 --> 01:30:07.123
This is going straight to YouTube.
Transformer vs. Sissy.


01:30:10.039 --> 01:30:12.580
She's going to kill him!


01:30:13.955 --> 01:30:15.664
Juanito!


01:30:26.121 --> 01:30:28.704
<i>Look out, danger.
The ball on the right side.</i>


01:30:28.788 --> 01:30:30.454
<i>It'll reach Leo Messi, Leo...</i>


01:30:30.621 --> 01:30:32.538
<i>Ball to the goalie, but look out,
there's a field-crasher.</i>


01:30:32.663 --> 01:30:33.538
Who's that?


01:30:33.704 --> 01:30:37.329
<i>Someone's down on the pitch,
but not a player, a field-crasher.</i>


01:30:37.413 --> 01:30:40.288
What a shitty field-crasher!


01:30:41.163 --> 01:30:42.538
He's not even naked!


01:30:42.829 --> 01:30:44.913
<i>He confronts the referee
and tells him it's a penalty.</i>


01:30:45.079 --> 01:30:48.412
<i>We can't believe it. We are all puzzled.</i>


01:30:48.578 --> 01:30:50.412
<i>What's this guy doing?
Get him off the field!</i>


01:30:50.578 --> 01:30:53.037
Throw him off the field, ref!


01:30:53.203 --> 01:30:55.412
He's going to fuck up the final.


01:30:55.578 --> 01:30:57.245
<i>It's incredible.
Look at the players' faces.</i>


01:30:57.328 --> 01:31:00.203
<i>He's grabbing the net.
Someone get this guy off!</i>


01:31:09.995 --> 01:31:11.662
Guys, look.


01:31:35.660 --> 01:31:38.161
-What are you doing here?
-Don't ask.


01:31:41.451 --> 01:31:44.951
-What have you done with my parents?
-I told you, they're not your parents.


01:31:55.284 --> 01:31:56.659
No, no, no!


01:32:03.783 --> 01:32:04.741
Jaime.


01:32:05.908 --> 01:32:07.699
Jaime, help me.
You have to distract her.


01:32:07.783 --> 01:32:09.534
I'm sorry, the robot?


01:32:09.617 --> 01:32:11.284
-You're crazy.
-She's going to destroy him!


01:32:11.450 --> 01:32:13.617
-But we can't do anything.
-Of course we can!


01:32:13.700 --> 01:32:16.574
-Distract her somehow!
-Wait, wait.


01:32:17.199 --> 01:32:18.283
I have a better plan.


01:32:18.616 --> 01:32:21.824
You and I go down to the basement
and stay there a couple of days.


01:32:21.908 --> 01:32:24.741
What? Are you trying
something with me, Jaime?


01:32:25.199 --> 01:32:26.699
But I was very subtle.


01:32:29.907 --> 01:32:31.782
Shit, shit! Shit!


01:32:32.407 --> 01:32:34.740
This is the famous ultimate weapon.


01:32:34.823 --> 01:32:38.907
Okay. I'd keep playing,
but I have a planet to destroy.


01:32:46.573 --> 01:32:47.615
Hey, Agata!


01:32:48.407 --> 01:32:51.073
Here, read my mind!


01:32:51.157 --> 01:32:54.406
I'm thinking you should follow me!


01:33:01.114 --> 01:33:02.697
-Grab something.
-It's too soft in here.


01:33:02.864 --> 01:33:04.197
-Up!
-I can't, Juan.


01:33:04.364 --> 01:33:05.697
Up!


01:33:08.196 --> 01:33:09.821
I almost distracted her.


01:33:10.030 --> 01:33:12.446
-What...?
-Juan, you're useless!


01:33:12.530 --> 01:33:13.864
Piece of shit!


01:33:13.947 --> 01:33:16.572
Hey, insult my son again
and you're screwed!


01:33:17.197 --> 01:33:19.655
I know it sounds weird, but it works.


01:33:19.738 --> 01:33:22.946
Juan, you're ugly! Real ugly!


01:33:23.363 --> 01:33:26.238
We all pull together
or the planet's screwed!


01:33:34.779 --> 01:33:35.612
Juan!


01:33:36.279 --> 01:33:37.654
Juan!


01:33:38.820 --> 01:33:40.237
Juan, get up!


01:33:46.070 --> 01:33:50.279
Juanito, an adopted child
isn't loved like a real one.


01:33:50.362 --> 01:33:53.820
-You're getting beaten by a girl!
-Get up, Juan!


01:33:53.987 --> 01:33:57.569
Juan! Help!


01:34:02.736 --> 01:34:03.861
Juan, I'm here!


01:34:38.901 --> 01:34:42.734
-Fine. Let's end this.
-I agree!


01:35:01.775 --> 01:35:03.316
Like on our first date, Juan!


01:35:05.316 --> 01:35:07.483
Blow her down in one!


01:35:16.357 --> 01:35:20.525
Luisa grabbed my ass a while ago!
Your mom's grabbing it now!


01:35:47.023 --> 01:35:50.064
-I can blow you down in one.
-Don't play the hero, Lopez.


01:35:50.148 --> 01:35:51.313
It's not your thing.


01:35:51.981 --> 01:35:53.939
My name is Superlopez.


01:36:23.146 --> 01:36:26.980
-Did he say Superlopez?
-I liked Sissy more.


01:36:29.646 --> 01:36:31.104
-Help!
-Juan...


01:36:31.271 --> 01:36:32.229
Are you alright?


01:36:32.312 --> 01:36:34.354
Get me out of here!


01:36:37.021 --> 01:36:38.437
-Are you alright?
-No, I'm not.


01:36:38.521 --> 01:36:39.437
-That's it.
-How awful.


01:36:39.604 --> 01:36:42.520
You're welcome, Juanito.
Second time I've saved you.


01:36:42.978 --> 01:36:43.728
-Son.
-Son.


01:36:43.811 --> 01:36:45.353
I almost got killed!


01:36:46.895 --> 01:36:49.478
Son, your father almost drowned.


01:36:49.645 --> 01:36:50.770
It was terrible.


01:36:52.645 --> 01:36:54.602
You've left me with no hats.


01:37:03.020 --> 01:37:04.061
Well...


01:37:04.228 --> 01:37:06.645
You saw what I did, right?


01:37:06.728 --> 01:37:08.727
Maybe you are a bit of a superhero.


01:37:09.560 --> 01:37:12.810
Maybe, yes.
What do we do now?


01:37:13.894 --> 01:37:18.394
-And landing in that pose.
-Yes, it wasn't on purpose.


01:37:18.477 --> 01:37:20.976
I don't know if you'll get used to it.


01:37:21.976 --> 01:37:22.934
What choice is there?


01:37:23.018 --> 01:37:25.559
Just thinking about it
gives me a knot in my gullet.


01:37:25.643 --> 01:37:29.769
But your real parents on Chiton
are waiting for you to save them.


01:37:30.477 --> 01:37:31.435
Don't worry, Mom.


01:37:33.226 --> 01:37:34.684
I've got it all under control.


01:37:50.683 --> 01:37:53.392
<i>My son, it's been so long.</i>


01:37:53.475 --> 01:37:55.225
Thanks to you, son,


01:37:55.392 --> 01:37:58.975
Chiton will finally be a free planet.


01:37:59.183 --> 01:38:02.100
Son, we've missed you so much.


01:38:02.642 --> 01:38:04.392
We knew you'd come back!


01:38:13.641 --> 01:38:16.349
Come, son. Give me a kiss.


01:38:26.598 --> 01:38:28.515
PLANET: CHITON
LEADER: ADMIRAL SKORBA


01:38:29.056 --> 01:38:31.266
LEADER: JEFERSON NORUEGA


01:39:37.179 --> 01:39:38.720
<i>Good morning. We awake today</i>


01:39:38.887 --> 01:39:41.720
<i>with the news of the emergence
of this strange superhero.</i>


01:39:41.803 --> 01:39:44.220
<i>Images of him have gone viral.</i>


01:39:44.303 --> 01:39:46.845
<i>City Hall is raising taxes</i>


01:39:46.928 --> 01:39:49.262
<i>to pay for the destruction in the city.</i>


01:39:49.428 --> 01:39:51.886
<i>And we have to add
another headache to this.</i>


01:39:51.969 --> 01:39:56.469
<i>Indeed, there's the stoppage
on Line 1 due to the accident</i>


01:39:56.636 --> 01:40:01.011
<i>and protests by fans
at the suspension of the Cup Final.</i>


01:40:01.094 --> 01:40:04.301
<i>Lots of listener messages
on our answering machine.</i>


01:40:04.676 --> 01:40:09.344
<i>This country, Spain,
has had real superheroes,</i>


01:40:09.427 --> 01:40:12.094
<i>like Don Pelayo, like El Cid,</i>


01:40:12.261 --> 01:40:15.427
<i>we don't deserve some guy
flying around in a leotard.</i>


01:40:16.011 --> 01:40:19.718
<i>I think this superhero
is a smokescreen</i>


01:40:19.885 --> 01:40:22.426
<i>so we don't talk about
what really matters.</i>


01:40:22.635 --> 01:40:26.426
<i>I'm 86, a widow for 40 years.</i>


01:40:26.593 --> 01:40:28.426
<i>I've fantasized about making love</i>


01:40:28.593 --> 01:40:31.425
<i>to all the superheroes
in alphabetical order.</i>


01:40:31.509 --> 01:40:34.217
<i>Can you believe that
this Spanish superhero</i>


01:40:34.300 --> 01:40:36.050
<i>arouses no desire in me?</i>


01:40:36.217 --> 01:40:39.343
<i>He looks so skinny,
so scrawny, so ugly,</i>


01:40:39.510 --> 01:40:43.925
<i>with that ridiculous name...
What is it? What's he called?</i>


01:41:04.174 --> 01:41:04.883
Don't start.


01:41:04.966 --> 01:41:07.840
-You always do this to me, Juan!
-What do you want me to do?


01:41:08.215 --> 01:41:11.799
I saw a column of smoke
and my body said: save humanity.


01:41:11.883 --> 01:41:13.299
Now it's fires too.


01:41:13.383 --> 01:41:16.216
When it's not a fire, it's a robbery,
or that boat the other day.


01:41:16.299 --> 01:41:18.216
Luisa, it was a cruise ship
and it was sinking.


01:41:18.299 --> 01:41:21.673
Sorry, whatever. Now it's smoke!
There are firemen!


01:41:21.757 --> 01:41:24.715
When I see someone in imminent danger,


01:41:24.798 --> 01:41:28.507
naturally I save them.
If I don't, I think that's terrible.


01:41:28.590 --> 01:41:30.298
So what do I have to do
to get you to come on time?


01:41:30.382 --> 01:41:31.673
Set fire to the restaurant?


01:41:32.007 --> 01:41:34.922
I've been late twice. 15 minutes
to save the planet and look how you get.


01:41:35.006 --> 01:41:37.256
Look, Juan, I'll tell you. As of now,


01:41:37.422 --> 01:41:40.631
you're going to have to combine
your superhero life with life in a couple.


01:41:40.714 --> 01:41:44.632
I'll tell you:
if there's a catastrophe and I do nothing,


01:41:45.381 --> 01:41:46.339
it's your fault!


01:41:48.631 --> 01:41:50.422
-Fine.
-Fine.


01:41:51.756 --> 01:41:52.922
Get the bill, go on.


01:41:57.756 --> 01:42:01.755
-Waiter, check, please.
-The man at the bar is buying.


01:42:13.421 --> 01:42:16.463
You owe me one, Superlopez.


01:46:42.325 --> 01:46:45.992
Translation: Lindsay Moxham

